{"parentUuid":"bee24bde-76a3-4d30-aac7-d869ae38cda5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- sanity-best-practices: Sanity development best practices for schema design, GROQ queries, TypeGen, Visual Editing, images, Portable Text, Studio structure, localization, migrations, Sanity Functions, Blueprints, and framework integrations such as Next.js, Nuxt, Astro, Remix, SvelteKit, Angular, Hydrogen, and the App SDK. Use this skill whenever working with Sanity schemas, defineType or defineField, GROQ or defineQuery, content modeling, Presentation or preview setups, Sanity-powered frontend integrations, Sanity Functions, documentEventHandler, defineDocumentFunction, defineMediaLibraryAssetFunction, @sanity/functions, @sanity/blueprints, sanity.blueprint.ts, event-driven content automation, or when reviewing and fixing a Sanity codebase.\n- sanity-migration: Plans, implements, and reviews migrations from other CMSes and content systems into Sanity. Use when migrating or replatforming to Sanity from AEM, Adobe Experience Manager, Contentful, Strapi, Webflow, WordPress, Payload, Drupal, Markdown/MDX/frontmatter files, WXR/XML exports, CMS APIs, database dumps, static HTML, or when designing extraction, transformation, Portable Text conversion, asset migration, redirects, validation, and cutover workflows.\n- ui-design:color-palette: Run the full colour workflow — tonal scales, semantic mapping, contrast checks, dark mode, and chart colours — and output a documented palette.\n- ui-design:design-screen: Design a complete screen layout from a description or requirements.\n- ui-design:platform-audit: Audit a design for iOS and Android convention compliance — navigation, controls, typography, and platform-specific gaps.\n- ui-design:responsive-audit: Audit a design's responsive behaviour across breakpoints — layout, touch targets, and content reflow.\n- ui-design:type-system: Build a typography system end to end — scale, weights, line heights, measure, and responsive behaviour.\n- design-systems:audit-system: Run a comprehensive audit of an existing design system for consistency, completeness, and accessibility.\n- design-systems:create-component: Scaffold a full component specification end to end — props, states, variants, accessibility, and documentation.\n- design-systems:tokenize: Extract tokens from an existing design or stylesheet and organise them — naming, structure, and theme mapping.\n- interaction-design:design-form: Design a form end to end — structure, decision points, chunking, validation, errors, and completion.\n- interaction-design:design-interaction: Design a complete interaction flow for a feature or component.\n- interaction-design:design-onboarding: Design a first-run experience end to end — activation path, progressive disclosure, and time to first value.\n- interaction-design:error-flow: Design an error flow end to end — prevention, detection, messaging, and recovery paths.\n- interaction-design:map-states: Model a component's states and transitions end to end — states, events, guards, and edge cases.\n- visual-critique:critique-screen: Run all seven visual critiques on a screen and output a prioritised fix list.\n- visual-critique:critique-ux: Run a focused UX critique on a screen — affordances, information density, and hierarchy — and output a prioritised fix list.\n- design-research:discover: Run a full user research cycle — persona creation, empathy mapping, and journey mapping for a product or feature.\n- design-research:interview: Prepare an interview script or summarize an interview transcript into structured insights.\n- design-research:synthesize: Synthesize research data into affinity diagrams, themes, and actionable insights.\n- design-research:test-plan: Run the full usability study workflow — research questions, participant criteria, tasks, metrics, and facilitation guide.\n- ux-strategy:benchmark: Run a competitive benchmark across a set of products — pattern comparison, gap analysis, and opportunity callouts.\n- ux-strategy:frame-problem: Structure an ambiguous design challenge into a clear problem definition with constraints and criteria.\n- ux-strategy:strategize: Develop a complete UX strategy for a product or feature area.\n- prototyping-testing:evaluate: Run a heuristic evaluation end to end — expert review against heuristics with severity ratings and recommended fixes.\n- prototyping-testing:experiment: Design an A/B experiment end to end — hypothesis, variants, primary metric, and sample size.\n- prototyping-testing:prototype-plan: Create a prototyping and testing plan for a design initiative.\n- prototyping-testing:test-plan: Choose a testing method and build the plan around it — method selection, task scenarios, click tests, and accessibility coverage.\n- design-ops:handoff: Run the full handoff workflow — specs, measurements, assets, states, and a QA checklist — and output a developer-ready package.\n- design-ops:plan-sprint: Run a design sprint end to end — challenge framing, schedule, exercises, and prototype test plan.\n- design-ops:setup-workflow: Set up a team's operating rhythm end to end — rituals, task flow, tooling, review gates, and version control.\n- designer-toolkit:build-presentation: Build a design presentation end to end — audience framing, narrative structure, and supporting rationale.\n- designer-toolkit:write-case-study: Build a portfolio case study end to end — project framing, process narrative, outcomes, and visuals.\n- designer-toolkit:write-rationale: Write design rationale for a set of decisions, linking each to user needs, business goals, and principles.\n- program-planning:plan-program: Stand up a new UX program end to end.\n- program-planning:reprioritise: Re-prioritise the program backlog after a change.\n- stakeholder-comms:align-stakeholders: Plan and run a stakeholder alignment session.\n- stakeholder-comms:report-status: Generate a full status update for the program.\n- delivery-execution:readiness-review: Run a launch readiness review.\n- delivery-execution:run-cycle: Orchestrate a delivery cycle from plan to retro.\n- cross-functional-alignment:clarify-roles: Produce a RACI and working agreement for a program.\n- cross-functional-alignment:set-up-intake: Stand up an intake and triage system.\n- measurement-ops:define-metrics: Define a measurement framework for the program.\n- measurement-ops:report-impact: Compile an impact report for leadership.\n- process-design:design-workflow: Design or redesign a team workflow.\n- process-design:scale-program: Build a scaling playbook for a proven approach.\n- people-management:prep-one-on-one: Prepare a meaningful 1:1.\n- people-management:run-review-cycle: Run a performance review cycle for the team.\n- team-building:onboard-hire: Build an onboarding plan for a new hire.\n- team-building:open-a-role: Define a role and stand up the hiring loop.\n- design-strategy:make-the-case: Build an investment case for design.\n- design-strategy:set-strategy: Develop a design strategy end to end.\n- org-influence:build-narrative: Build an executive narrative to win support.\n- org-influence:secure-resources: Prepare a headcount or budget ask.\n- operating-cadence:run-design-review: Run a scaled design review process.\n- operating-cadence:set-cadence: Design the team's operating cadence.\n- leadership-craft:lead-change: Plan and lead a change initiative.\n- leadership-craft:resolve-conflict: Work through a team conflict.\n- model-interaction-design:audit-interaction: Evaluate an existing AI interaction against interaction mode taxonomies.\n- model-interaction-design:design-conversation: Design a complete human-AI conversation flow for a feature.\n- model-interaction-design:map-initiative: Map who leads at each stage of an AI-powered workflow.\n- ai-alignment-reasoning:design-guardrails: Create a complete guardrail specification for an AI feature.\n- ai-alignment-reasoning:red-team: Run a structured red-teaming exercise to find alignment failures.\n- ai-alignment-reasoning:write-policy: Draft an AI behavior policy covering safety, tone, and boundaries.\n- system-behavior-shaping:calibrate-tone: Develop a tone matrix mapping contexts to appropriate AI behavior.\n- system-behavior-shaping:design-persona: Create a complete AI persona specification with voice, tone, and behavioral rules.\n- system-behavior-shaping:stress-test: Test an AI persona against edge cases, adversarial inputs, and emotional scenarios.\n- evaluation:create-rubric: Build a scoring rubric for evaluating AI output quality.\n- evaluation:design-benchmark: Design a benchmark suite to measure AI product performance over time.\n- evaluation:run-evaluation: Execute a structured evaluation of an AI feature against defined criteria.\n- design-agent-orchestration:design-oversight: Create a human oversight plan for an agentic system.\n- design-agent-orchestration:design-workflow: Design a complete multi-agent workflow with roles, handoffs, and fallbacks.\n- design-agent-orchestration:map-agents: Map out agent responsibilities, boundaries, and communication patterns.\n- prompt-architecture:audit-prompt: Evaluate an existing prompt for clarity, effectiveness, and edge cases.\n- prompt-architecture:build-chain: Design a multi-step prompt chain for a complex task.\n- prompt-architecture:design-prompt: Create a structured system prompt for an AI feature.\n- ui-design:aesthetic-usability: Apply the Aesthetic-Usability Effect — polished, consistent interfaces are perceived as more usable and forgive minor friction. Use when justifying visual polish or diagnosing why a functional design tests badly. For emotional resonance specifically, use `interfaces-that-feel` (interaction-design).\n- ui-design:color-system: Build a product colour system — tonal scales, semantic roles, and contrast compliance. Use when defining or rebuilding colour from scratch. For dark-mode adaptation use `dark-mode-design`; for chart palettes use `data-visualization`; for multi-brand token architecture use `theming-system` (design-systems).\n- ui-design:dark-mode-design: Adapt an existing palette to dark mode — surface elevation, contrast rebalancing, and desaturation rules. Use when you already have a light palette to translate. For building the base palette first, use `color-system`.\n- ui-design:data-visualization: Select chart types and design data encodings — marks, axes, labels, and accessible chart styling. Use when presenting data graphically. Owns chart selection and encoding only; the categorical colour ramp itself belongs to `color-system`.\n- ui-design:illustration-style: Define an illustration style guide — visual language, colour usage, and application rules. Use when commissioning or standardising illustration. For icons, use `icon-system` (design-systems).\n- ui-design:law-of-closure: Apply the Law of Closure — the eye completes implied shapes from partial forms. Use when reducing visual weight by dropping borders or letting negative space suggest structure. For explicit containers, use `law-of-common-region`.\n- ui-design:law-of-common-region: Apply the Law of Common Region — a shared container, background, or border groups elements regardless of spacing. Use when grouping must survive a tight layout. For grouping by spacing alone, use `law-of-proximity`.\n- ui-design:law-of-continuity\n- ui-design:law-of-figure-ground\n- ui-design:law-of-proximity\n- ui-design:law-of-similarity\n- ui-design:layout-grid\n- ui-design:platform-conventions\n- ui-design:readable-measure\n- ui-design:responsive-design\n- ui-design:spacing-system\n- ui-design:typography-scale\n- ui-design:visual-hierarchy\n- ui-design:von-restorff-effect\n- design-systems:accessibility-audit\n- design-systems:component-spec\n- design-systems:design-system-governance\n- design-systems:design-token\n- design-systems:documentation-template\n- design-systems:icon-system\n- design-systems:localization-design\n- design-systems:motion-system\n- design-systems:naming-convention\n- design-systems:pattern-library\n- design-systems:theming-system\n- interaction-design:animation-principles\n- interaction-design:conversational-ux\n- interaction-design:doherty-threshold\n- interaction-design:error-handling-ux\n- interaction-design:feedback-patterns\n- interaction-design:fitts-law\n- interaction-design:form-design\n- interaction-design:gesture-patterns\n- interaction-design:hicks-law\n- interaction-design:interfaces-that-feel\n- interaction-design:jakobs-law\n- interaction-design:loading-states\n- interaction-design:micro-interaction-spec\n- interaction-design:millers-law\n- interaction-design:navigation-patterns\n- interaction-design:onboarding-design\n- interaction-design:peak-end-rule\n- interaction-design:search-ux\n- interaction-design:serial-position-effect\n- interaction-design:state-machine\n- interaction-design:teslers-law\n- interaction-design:zeigarnik-effect\n- visual-critique:critique-affordance\n- visual-critique:critique-brand-consistency\n- visual-critique:critique-color\n- visual-critique:critique-composition\n- visual-critique:critique-information-density\n- visual-critique:critique-typography\n- visual-critique:critique-visual-hierarchy\n- design-research:affinity-diagram\n- design-research:card-sort-analysis\n- design-research:diary-study-plan\n- design-research:empathy-map\n- design-research:interview-script\n- design-research:jobs-to-be-done\n- design-research:journey-map\n- design-research:research-repository\n- design-research:summarize-interview\n- design-research:survey-design\n- design-research:usability-test-plan\n- design-research:user-persona\n- ux-strategy:business-design\n- ux-strategy:competitive-analysis\n- ux-strategy:content-strategy\n- ux-strategy:design-brief\n- ux-strategy:design-principles\n- ux-strategy:experience-map\n- ux-strategy:information-architecture\n- ux-strategy:metrics-definition\n- ux-strategy:north-star-vision\n- ux-strategy:opportunity-framework\n- ux-strategy:service-b