{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","bridgeSessionId":"cse_019EmTaH39trFL1Hsyb3xmBc","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"4863d667-5619-446a-b023-2ef269cc168d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"4736e0a4-4532-439e-9626-cb2afa39fc52"}
{"parentUuid":"f78aa4b4-46ed-4a1a-9480-d58d97fc7777","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemXfLCXi6TtbrCAwABMU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The server is back up and the site renders clean.\n\n**http://127.0.0.1:8412/** — working again, all six pages, no console errors.\n\nWhat happened: the preview server died when the last session ended, and the script that ran it lived in that session's scratchpad, which got cleaned up with it. I've recreated it in this session's scratchpad and restarted it. It still sends `no-store`, so you won't get a stale cached version.\n\nNothing about the site itself changed — this was just getting the link working again. The paper redesign from the last commit (`5eeed0d`) is what you'll see: ink on bone, red accent, the big serif headline, and the map as a hairline chart rather than a glow.\n\nMy question from before still stands, and I'd rather not guess a fourth time. When you're up, tell me which of these it is:\n\n- **Direction is right, keep going** — then I'd fix the map page hero, the section density, and 390px, which I know are the weak spots.\n- **Direction is wrong** — and specifically whether it's the light-on-paper choice, the typography, the map treatment, or the whole structure.\n\nThe full-page renders of all six pages are in `umbra/docs/renders/paper-*.png` if it's easier to flip through those than scroll the live site."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1925,"cache_read_input_tokens":731014,"output_tokens":399,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1925,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":731014,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1925},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CemXdkcezHUjXAAH76v97","type":"assistant","uuid":"7a9721dc-3333-4919-9f3d-684dceeaff90","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:09:19.742Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"7a9721dc-3333-4919-9f3d-684dceeaff90","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":1,"hookInfos":[{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":1839}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:09:21.688Z","uuid":"48eef85a-c193-4907-b7b6-499d96da4e0c","toolUseID":"2eb2c096-da5e-4d32-8948-0e649dc7700f","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"48eef85a-c193-4907-b7b6-499d96da4e0c","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"turn_duration","durationMs":158485,"messageCount":1406,"timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:09:21.699Z","uuid":"9c62345d-0dd7-49b2-aedb-eef7c75931bc","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"9c62345d-0dd7-49b2-aedb-eef7c75931bc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d8a2ec20-ec1e-497e-a80e-02dc85fe39b9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"It is buildathon day, 6 September. All times IST: kickoff 9:00, stable state by\n11:45, Curveball at 12:00, submission 15:00. Read umbra/NOTES.md, umbra/PUBLISH.md\nand scripts/graft.sh in the existing Umbra repository before you start.\n\nTrack: E2, Graph Intelligence. Upstream is entireio/entire-graph on main (public,\nMIT). Umbra lives in umbra/ as its own Go module and never imports entire-graph\npackages.\n\nDo NOT push the old repository's checkpoint refs to the new mirror. The new\nremote starts clean and stays clean. Do not run entire configure with a\ncheckpoint-remote pointing at the old repo.\n\nNo em dashes in anything you write. go test ./... green before every commit.\n\nSTEP 1, the mirror workflow. Fork entireio/entire-graph, then:\n  entire login\n  entire repo mirror create\n  entire repo clone /gh/u7k4rs6/entire-graph\nSelect the fork and the India region at the prompt; it is a prompt, not a flag.\nClone under $HOME, never a scratch or sandbox directory, or Graph refuses the\nrepository metadata. Then:\n  entire enable -y --agent claude-code\n  entire status\nConfirm entire status names the new remote before any commit. Work only inside\nthis clone from here on.\n\nSTEP 2, the plugin. The upstream README's install path is:\n  go install github.com/entireio/entire-graph/cmd/entire-graph@main\n  entire plugin install \"$(go env GOPATH)/bin/entire-graph\" --force\nThis needs a Go toolchain with CGO because tree-sitter uses native bindings, so\nit may take several minutes. If the build fails, fall back to the release\narchive rather than debugging cgo. Then:\n  entire graph version\n  entire graph doctor --json\n  entire graph init-agents --repo .\nRecord the doctor output. It reports no_egress=true directly, which is a better\nsource for the offline assertion than inferring it from capabilities; switch that\ntest over if it is quick.\n\nSTEP 3, verify the field before trusting anything. Upstream documents indexing\nprofiles: syntax-only emits only DEFINES and CONTAINS, fast adds shallow calls\nand boundaries, full emits every relation type. Umbra's field needs CALLS,\nUSES_TYPE, DATA_FLOWS, TESTS and FILE_CHANGES_WITH. Run\n  entire graph capabilities --json\nand check which relations this build actually emits by default. If the default is\nnot full, find the flag that makes Umbra's snapshot and impact calls request it,\nand note it. If the relations Umbra needs are unavailable, that is a degradation,\nnot an error: apply the degradation table and say so in the header. Do this\nbefore the demo run, because thin relations mean wrong demo numbers.\n\nSTEP 4, first commit: the four planning documents plus HANDOFF.md and\nKICKOFF_PROMPT.md only, no product code. Create the \"initial understanding and\nintended architecture\" checkpoint against it. The checkpoint must carry real\nreasoning: the four states, why the subtraction is the product, the settled\ndecisions, and the rejected options from NOTES.md.\n\nSTEP 5, second commit: the product code as one clearly labelled import commit,\nwith NOTES.md and the corrections list. Do not fabricate a phase-by-phase history\nthat did not happen in this repository. Then verify the graft:\n  go test ./...\n  entire umbra HEAD --test \"pytest -v\" --out ./out\nagainst the fixture app. The claim to match exactly: 8 probes selected, 5 cracked,\nfull sweep, 0 leaks. If the numbers differ in this clone, find out why before\n11:00 and write the reason down. Never use pytest -q; it degrades verify to\nexit-code-only.\n\nSTEP 6, graph evidence, recorded as you go, worth 15 points:\n  one entire graph search or def lookup\n  one entire graph impact analysis run before a change you then make\n  entire graph diff --base <first commit> --head HEAD as the final semantic diff\nWrite each into BUILDATHON.md with what it found and how you verified it against\nsource and tests. Graph output is evidence, not an oracle; never present an\nuncertain finding as fact.\n\nSTEP 7, BUILDATHON.md in the repository root, using the participant guide's exact\noutline: name, one-sentence summary, problem and intended user, selected track and\nwhy Entire is essential, architecture and main workflow, Graph findings and\nverification, Noon Curveball, checkpoint links and what each proves, setup and\nrun and test instructions, known limitations and next steps. Fill everything now\nexcept the Curveball section. Limitations must include: the examined set comes\nfrom tool activity so shell-driven agents leave little trace; the stale-worktree\nfailure mode and where to delete; that checks are only trusted once observed\nfailing; and that umbra clean is documented but not built.\n\nSTEP 8, by 11:45: stop adding anything. Runnable state committed, tests green,\npre-noon checkpoint created recording current intent, architecture, completed\nwork, unresolved work and technical risks. Do not start after 11:00 anything you\ncannot finish by 11:45.\n\nSTEP 9, at 12:00: close the session. Read the Constraint-change playbook in\nARCHITECTURE.md. Write a short plan into NOTES.md before editing. Run\nentire graph impact on the affected area first. Implement the smallest complete\nresponse inside the boundary the playbook names, test the changed behaviour, and\ncommit it as its own checkpoint. Then fill the Curveball section of BUILDATHON.md\nwith what changed, why the revised behaviour can be trusted, and the test that\nproves it.\n\nSTEP 10, final 20 minutes: final commit pushed and the SHA recorded, project\nlaunches from a clean checkout via the documented path, four checkpoints open and\nexplain their milestones, semantic diff recorded, BUILDATHON.md complete and free\nof secrets, tests covering the critical and Curveball behaviour green, fallback\nscreenshots available locally.\n\nReport at 11:00 with: mirror and plugin working yes or no, which relations the\ncapabilities call reports, the demo numbers observed, which graph evidence is\nrecorded, and which BUILDATHON.md sections are still empty."},"uuid":"e169dbc0-1618-41e3-8fa8-f40b8734516b","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:12:02.620Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
