{"parentUuid":"2dfef7a7-765b-49b2-8033-712d74f1c7e6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemYED8JJPjkzaNnmTwfD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PNUp7FihCRD8ziY7u6wE8P","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd $HOME\necho \"=== mirror create ===\"; entire repo mirror create --help 2>&1 | head -22\necho; echo \"=== repo clone ===\"; entire repo clone --help 2>&1 | head -20","description":"Inspect mirror create and repo clone"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":756,"cache_read_input_tokens":737930,"output_tokens":661,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":443},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":756,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":661,"cache_read_input_tokens":737930,"cache_creation_input_tokens":756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":756},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CemYE2SMs8LY8ZvBmVsZi","type":"assistant","uuid":"0124d31a-ae09-43e6-b39b-21881c37a0de","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:16:47.413Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"0124d31a-ae09-43e6-b39b-21881c37a0de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"97c900fd-bfa8-444f-9355-c54cc2103e2a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNUp7FihCRD8ziY7u6wE8P","type":"tool_result","content":"=== mirror create ===\nWith no arguments, launches an interactive wizard: pick repos to mirror, pick one or more regions, then creates every (repo, region) mirror in parallel and prints the clone URLs.\n\nWith a <github-url>, registers a mirror placement for that repo on the target cluster, then waits for the initial GitHub→EntireDB clone to finish so `git clone` works on return. Pass --no-wait to return as soon as the placement is registered. Idempotent on (upstream, cluster). When the cluster-host is omitted, an interactive terminal offers the available clusters as a picker; non-interactive runs default to aws-us-east-2.entire.io.\n\nMirror creation uses the asynchronous request route by default. Set async_mirror_requests to false in the layered settings to use the synchronous route.\n\nUsage:\n  entire repo mirror create [github-url] [cluster-host] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire repo mirror create\n  entire repo mirror create github.com/octocat/hello-world\n  entire repo mirror create github.com/octocat/hello-world aws-us-east-2.entire.io\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help                    help for create\n      --no-wait                 Return once the placement is registered, without waiting for the initial clone\n      --wait-timeout duration   How long to wait. Async mode applies one deadline to request submission, placement, and clone readiness; synchronous mode applies it only to clone readiness (default 30m0s)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\n=== repo clone ===\nClone an Entire-native repo by its `/et/<project>/<repo>` ref, a GitHub mirror by its `/gh/<owner>/<repo>` ref, or a full `entire://` clone URL.\n\nA native ref resolves the repo's home cluster and clones from there (--cluster doesn't apply).\n\nWith a `/gh/<owner>/<repo>` ref, looks up where the repo is mirrored: if it's on a single cluster, clones it directly; if it's mirrored on more than one, prompts you to pick which to clone from (or pass --cluster to choose non-interactively).\n\nA full `entire://` URL already names the cluster, so it's passed straight through to `git clone` with no lookup (and --cluster is ignored). The optional [target-dir] is passed through to `git clone` either way.\n\nUsage:\n  entire repo clone <repo> [target-dir] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire repo clone /et/project/example\n  entire repo clone /gh/entirehq/entire-api\n  entire repo clone /gh/entirehq/entire-api ./entire-api\n  entire repo clone /gh/entirehq/entire-api --cluster aws-us-east-2.entire.io\n  entire repo clone entire://aws-us-east-2.entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire-api\n\nFlags:\n      --cluster string   Cluster host to clone from when the repo is mirrored on more than one (may belong to another auth context)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"49317cd8-af36-48ec-8911-5925fa8c6b21","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:16:49.751Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== mirror create ===\nWith no arguments, launches an interactive wizard: pick repos to mirror, pick one or more regions, then creates every (repo, region) mirror in parallel and prints the clone URLs.\n\nWith a <github-url>, registers a mirror placement for that repo on the target cluster, then waits for the initial GitHub→EntireDB clone to finish so `git clone` works on return. Pass --no-wait to return as soon as the placement is registered. Idempotent on (upstream, cluster). When the cluster-host is omitted, an interactive terminal offers the available clusters as a picker; non-interactive runs default to aws-us-east-2.entire.io.\n\nMirror creation uses the asynchronous request route by default. Set async_mirror_requests to false in the layered settings to use the synchronous route.\n\nUsage:\n  entire repo mirror create [github-url] [cluster-host] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire repo mirror create\n  entire repo mirror create github.com/octocat/hello-world\n  entire repo mirror create github.com/octocat/hello-world aws-us-east-2.entire.io\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help                    help for create\n      --no-wait                 Return once the placement is registered, without waiting for the initial clone\n      --wait-timeout duration   How long to wait. Async mode applies one deadline to request submission, placement, and clone readiness; synchronous mode applies it only to clone readiness (default 30m0s)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n\n=== repo clone ===\nClone an Entire-native repo by its `/et/<project>/<repo>` ref, a GitHub mirror by its `/gh/<owner>/<repo>` ref, or a full `entire://` clone URL.\n\nA native ref resolves the repo's home cluster and clones from there (--cluster doesn't apply).\n\nWith a `/gh/<owner>/<repo>` ref, looks up where the repo is mirrored: if it's on a single cluster, clones it directly; if it's mirrored on more than one, prompts you to pick which to clone from (or pass --cluster to choose non-interactively).\n\nA full `entire://` URL already names the cluster, so it's passed straight through to `git clone` with no lookup (and --cluster is ignored). The optional [target-dir] is passed through to `git clone` either way.\n\nUsage:\n  entire repo clone <repo> [target-dir] [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire repo clone /et/project/example\n  entire repo clone /gh/entirehq/entire-api\n  entire repo clone /gh/entirehq/entire-api ./entire-api\n  entire repo clone /gh/entirehq/entire-api --cluster aws-us-east-2.entire.io\n  entire repo clone entire://aws-us-east-2.entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire-api\n\nFlags:\n      --cluster string   Cluster host to clone from when the repo is mirrored on more than one (may belong to another auth context)","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0124d31a-ae09-43e6-b39b-21881c37a0de","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
