{"parentUuid":"aa9be0be-274b-4076-b7af-fc39fc2a0dec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemYhpATRqVwtKhN1d9g2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that doesn't need login is done. I'm blocked on one interactive step.\n\n## What you need to run\n\n```\nentire login\n```\n\nThat's a browser OAuth flow, so I can't drive it. `entire auth contexts` currently reports no login contexts at all. Once you're logged in I'll take the mirror from there — `entire repo mirror create` accepts an explicit cluster host as an argument, so if I can enumerate the India cluster I'll do it non-interactively; if not, I'll hand the wizard back to you for the fork and region picks.\n\n## Answers to your five questions\n\n**1. Mirror and plugin working?** Plugin **yes**, mirror **no, not started**.\n\nThe fork exists: `u7k4rs6/entire-graph`, confirmed a fork of `entireio/entire-graph`, default branch `main`. The plugin built from source with CGO (84MB, tree-sitter compiled fine, no fallback to the release archive needed) and installed. `entire graph version` reports `dev`.\n\n`entire graph doctor --json` reports **`no_egress: true`** directly, plus every `phase_1_local_only` flag false and every `features_requiring_network_access` false. You're right that this is a better source than inferring from capabilities, and it's a one-line switch when I get to the test.\n\nThe mirror is untouched because it needs login. No `entire configure --checkpoint-remote` has been run, and nothing has been pushed anywhere.\n\n**2. Which relations the capabilities call reports.** The default profile is **`full`** on both `snapshot` and `impact`, and Umbra passes no `--profile` anywhere, so it already gets `full`. Profiles:\n\n| Profile | Umbra's five |\n|---|---|\n| `syntax-only` | none |\n| `fast` | CALLS only |\n| `full` | all five |\n\nI didn't stop at the table. A real snapshot of the repo (10,318 records) emits, repo-wide and in the fixture app: CALLS 1856/29, DATA_FLOWS 441/11, USES_TYPE 281/9, FILE_CHANGES_WITH 162/1, TESTS 11/2. **All five present. No degradation, no flag needed.**\n\nOne thing worth knowing: Python's `relation_support_by_language` entry omits TESTS and FILE_CHANGES_WITH, which looks alarming. It isn't. Those two are listed for **0 of 185 languages** because they're derived rather than parsed, TESTS heuristically and FILE_CHANGES_WITH from git co-change. The empirical count is what settles it.\n\n**3. Demo numbers observed.** Exact match, with the newly built plugin: **8 probes selected, 5 cracked, full sweep, 0 leaks**, naming both refund tests and the three service tests. `pytest -v`, never `-q`. `go test ./...` green across all nine packages.\n\n**4. Graph evidence recorded.** **None recorded yet**, because BUILDATHON.md belongs in the new clone. Of the three, `entire graph def` works and returns real output for `compute_total`. `entire graph search \"compute_total\"` was rejected with \"search received unexpected arguments\" — I'll find the correct syntax rather than guess. The impact-before-a-change and the final `graph diff` both need the new repo.\n\n**5. BUILDATHON.md sections still empty.** **All of them.** The file does not exist. It belongs in the mirror clone, which doesn't exist yet.\n\n## Two things I need a decision on\n\n**HANDOFF.md and KICKOFF_PROMPT.md do not exist.** Step 4 says commit them, but neither is in the repo. Earlier in this project you told me to ignore kickoff and handoff and that the kickoff prompt was your first message. I can reconstruct KICKOFF_PROMPT.md from your actual first message, which is real text you wrote. I will not invent a HANDOFF.md. Tell me which you want.\n\n**The module path has to change.** Umbra is `module github.com/u7k4rs6/Umbra/umbra` and inside the fork it becomes `github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra`. That's 43 Go files and 13 documentation references including the install command. Mechanical, but it happens during the import commit and the tests must be green after it. Flagging it so it isn't a surprise at 11:00.\n\nUmbra imports no entire-graph package, so the \"own Go module, never imports upstream\" requirement already holds."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_read_input_tokens":764625,"output_tokens":2311,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":836},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":2311,"cache_read_input_tokens":764625,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1371},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CemYhfdjyHypnAu94bQHp","type":"assistant","uuid":"da0fb3f0-f956-4451-a954-3a6c3d746e93","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:23:24.984Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra/umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
