{"parentUuid":"6f0f66ec-cbf1-448e-93d3-98f028421a51","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"47ecdd8a-ca00-4576-a9bb-909e9e5db54c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018SmupQZ2CseP2w24xGRsJu","type":"tool_result","content":"=== any cluster listing command? ===\nNavigation Flags:\n      --all                 Fetch the complete directory instead of the first 1000 entries (slower on large orgs)\n      --limit int           Show at most N rows, applied after the local filters and sort (0 shows all fetched)\n      --page-size int       Fetch a single page of at most N entries (1-500; the server may cap N further) and print the resume cursor\n      --page-token string   Fetch the single page at this cursor (from a previous run's nextPageToken)\n\nFiltering & Sorting Flags:\n  Applied only to the fetched rows; combine with --all to filter/sort the complete mirror list.\n      --access string    Filter by exact ACCESS (candidates only: read/write/admin)\n      --available        Keep only GitHub repos you could onboard as mirrors (drops existing mirrors)\n      --cluster string   Keep only repos mirrored on this cluster, by slug or public host (drops onboardable candidates)\n      --mirrored         Keep only repos already mirrored (drops onboardable candidates)\n\n=== try the api for clusters ===\nUsage:\n  entire api <path> [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire api /api/v1/clusters\n  entire api --to cell /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --jurisdiction eu /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --to cell \"/api/v1/me/recap?repo={repo_id}\"\n  entire api -X POST /api/v1/projects -f name=demo\n\nFlags:\n  -F, --field stringArray       add a typed parameter in key=value format; true/false/null/numbers are converted (repeatable)\n  -H, --header stringArray      add a request header in key:value format (repeatable)\n  -h, --help                    help for api\n  -i, --include                 print the response status line and headers too\n      --input string            file with the request body (\"-\" for stdin)\n  -j, --jurisdiction string     target a specific jurisdiction's cell (e.g. us, eu) instead of your home cell; implies --to cell\n  -X, --method string           HTTP method (default GET, or POST when a field/body is given)\n  -f, --raw-field stringArray   add a string parameter in key=value format (repeatable)\n      --to string               which backend to call: core or cell (default \"core\")\n\n--- alt path ---\nUsage:\n  entire api <path> [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  entire api /api/v1/clusters\n  entire api --to cell /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --jurisdiction eu /api/v1/me/activity\n  entire api --to cell \"/api/v1/me/recap?repo={repo_id}\"\n  entire api -X POST /api/v1/projects -f name=demo\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"65e42048-4d0d-45d7-a933-53bd3e6c84df","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:32:48.672Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== any cluster listing command? ===\nNavigation Flags:\n      --all                 Fetch the complete directory instead of the first 1000 entries (slower on large orgs)\n      --limit int           Show at most N rows, applied after the local filters and sort (0 shows all fetched)\n      --page-size int       Fetch a single page of at most N entries (1-500; the server may cap N further) and print the resume cursor\n      --page-token string   Fetch the single page at this cursor (from a previous run's nextPageToken)\n\nFiltering & Sorting Flags:\n  Applied only to the fetched rows; combine with --all to filter/sort the complete mirror list.\n      --access string    Filter by exact ACCESS (candidates only: read/write/admin)\n      --available        Keep only GitHub repos you could onboard as mirrors (drops existing mirrors)\n      --cluster string   Keep only repos mirrored on this cluster, by slug or public host (drops onboardable candidates)\n      --mirrored         Keep only repos already mirrored (drops onboardable candid