{"parentUuid":"f35e16f3-fa5e-4149-976a-c7946eae08e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemZW7iuyNqqcjYQuxvgL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018nN5RBT3G5fEebSrudRNcs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra\nentire graph search --help 2>&1 | head -28","description":"Find the correct graph search syntax"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":197,"cache_read_input_tokens":773251,"output_tokens":678,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":518},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":197,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":678,"cache_read_input_tokens":773251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":197,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":197},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CemZVxBC1bheY29ZUPDGo","type":"assistant","uuid":"b70a9c28-6288-40e8-a71c-bd23f776db80","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:33:30.173Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"b70a9c28-6288-40e8-a71c-bd23f776db80","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"47ecdd8a-ca00-4576-a9bb-909e9e5db54c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018nN5RBT3G5fEebSrudRNcs","type":"tool_result","content":"Find the code for a task from a plain-language query (start here)\n\nUsage:\n  entire graph search --query \"issue or concept\" --repo . [--top-k 10] [--format text|json|ndjson|agent] [--head] [--profile fast|full] [--deep]\n\nRanked source regions for a plain-language description, with source and file:line inline, budgeted to drop straight into context. This is the first move for almost every locate task.\n\nBy default search returns: ranked candidate fix sites (top hits as full function bodies), RELATED SITES, the COVERING TEST plus other tests over the same code (ALSO COVERING), SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL (every place the concept is named, tagged EDIT/CONSUMER/DOC), a VERIFY line (the narrowest test command for the file), and a CLOSED-SET WARNING when a switch over a sealed set would fail at runtime. The three reference blocks (container map, signature types, declaration card) are OFF by default because they cost turns in agent sessions; --reference-blocks all turns them on for interactive reading.\n\n--top-k only changes how many results come back; --deep additionally runs the exhaustive sparse (BM25) pass and fuses it with the semantic ranking (slower, reads every eligible file).\n\nRanking returns one region per unit, which is right for code and wrong for whole prose documents: one markdown document can hold the answer across several distant regions. So for prose the unit is the SECTION, not the file — a document's headed sections are ranked against every other section on their own scores, exactly as independent files would be (--document-resolution ranks a document as one unit instead). Separately, and on prose of any shape including headed documents, when fewer distinct units match than --top-k asked for, the spare slots are spent returning finer regions of the same document as results of their own (multi-resolution retrieval) — strictly additive, so it never displaces a unit and never breaches --max-context-bytes. --single-resolution turns that off. The two stack: a headed document can be ranked by section AND have spare slots filled with promoted passages, so a prose payload may carry both.\n\nFlags:\n  --query <text>            The task or bug in one plain sentence (required)\n  --repo <path>             Repository to search (default: current repo)\n  --top-k <n>               Number of results to return (default: 10)\n  --format text|json|ndjson|agent\n                            Output format; text is tiered for reading, agent is compact (default: json)\n  --head                    Search the committed tree (cached) instead of the working tree\n  --profile syntax-only|fast|full\n                            Parsing depth; use full for bug-fix/locate (call-graph active) (default: fast)\n  --deep                    Also run the exhaustive BM25 pass and fuse it (slower)\n  --single-resolution       One result per ranked unit; do not spend spare slots on finer regions of a prose document\n  --document-resolution     Rank a prose document as one unit; do not rank its sections separately\n  --max-context-bytes <n>   Output byte budget; 0 = unbounded (default: 24576)\n  --reference-blocks all|container-map,signature-types,type-card\n                            Turn reference blocks back on (off by default)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1a8fa1b1-5547-4691-b075-8e9a9c8d5624","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:33:32.651Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Find the code for a task from a plain-language query (start here)\n\nUsage:\n  entire graph search --query \"issue or concept\" --repo . [--top-k 10] [--format text|json|ndjson|agent] [--head] [--profile fast|full] [--deep]\n\nRanked source regions for a plain-language description, with source and file:line inline, budgeted to drop straight into context. This is the first move for almost every locate task.\n\nBy default search returns: ranked candidate fix sites (top hits as full function bodies), RELATED SITES, the COVERING TEST plus other tests over the same code (ALSO COVERING), SAME-CONCEPT LITERAL (every place the concept is named, tagged EDIT/CONSUMER/DOC), a VERIFY line (the narrowest test command for the file), and a CLOSED-SET WARNING when a switch over a sealed set would fail at runtime. The three reference blocks (container map, signature types, declaration card) are OFF by default because they cost turns in agent sessions; --reference-blocks all turns them on for interactive reading.\n\n--top-k only changes how many results come back; --deep additionally runs the exhaustive sparse (BM25) pass and fuses it with the semantic ranking (slower, reads every eligible file).\n\nRanking returns one region per unit, which is right for code and wrong for whole prose documents: one markdown document can hold the answer across several distant regions. So for prose the unit is the SECTION, not the file — a document's headed sections are ranked against every other section on their own scores, exactly as independent files would be (--document-resolution ranks a document as one unit instead). Separately, and on prose of any shape including headed documents, when fewer distinct units match than --top-k asked for, the spare slots are spent returning finer regions of the same document as results of their own (multi-resolution retrieval) — strictly additive, so it never displaces a unit and never breaches --max-context-bytes. --single-resolution turns that off. The two stack: a headed document can be ranked by section AND have spare slots filled with promoted passages, so a prose payload may carry both.\n\nFlags:\n  --query <text>            The task or bug in one plain sentence (required)\n  --repo <path>             Repository to search (default: current repo)\n  --top-k <n>               Number of results to return (default: 10)\n  --format text|json|ndjson|agent\n                            Output format; text is tiered for reading, agent is compact (default: json)\n  --head                    Search the committed tree (cached) instead of the working tree\n  --profile syntax-only|fast|full\n                            Parsing depth; use full for bug-fix/locate (call-graph active) (default: fast)\n  --deep                    Also run the exhaustive BM25 pass and fuse it (slower)\n  --single-resolution       One result per ranked unit; do not spend spare slots on finer regions of a prose document\n  --document-resolution     Rank a prose document as one unit; do not rank its sections separately\n  --max-context-bytes <n>   Output byte budget; 0 = unbounded (default: 24576)\n  --reference-blocks all|container-map,signature-types,type-card\n                            Turn reference blocks back on (off by default)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b70a9c28-6288-40e8-a71c-bd23f776db80","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
