{"parentUuid":"2f7a83ca-9c7c-4568-b457-a16b438f519a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemZfkDPcoPwAEWJ8YdTs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Docs copied clean. Now the two documents that didn't exist in the source repo — writing both honestly labelled rather than fabricating history."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2572,"cache_read_input_tokens":778595,"output_tokens":1348,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":308},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1348,"cache_read_input_tokens":778595,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2572},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CemZfdSLqjx6AvgNgBU6J","type":"assistant","uuid":"a20fb7d2-f6f4-41c0-8faf-b06bb3d4fa67","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:35:37.229Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"a20fb7d2-f6f4-41c0-8faf-b06bb3d4fa67","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemZfkDPcoPwAEWJ8YdTs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UDeavWPQT74q7ap7Jrot8j","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/utkuputku/entire-graph/umbra/KICKOFF_PROMPT.md","content":"# Kickoff prompt\n\nThis is the brief Umbra was built from, recorded here because the build never\nkept it as a file. It is reconstructed from the session record rather than\ncopied from an existing document, and it is placed in the first commit so the\nintent is in the repository before any code is.\n\n## The problem\n\nFind the code an AI agent's change affects but the agent never looked at.\n\nA clean diff and a confident description tell a reviewer what changed. They do\nnot tell the reviewer what the agent never opened. Umbra takes the dependents of\nevery changed symbol from Entire Graph, subtracts what the session actually\nexamined according to the checkpoint's tool activity and the agent's own words,\nranks what is left in shadow, runs the tests that reach it, and then sweeps the\nwhole suite once so the selection audits itself.\n\n## Settled decisions, not open questions\n\n- Go, one static binary named `entire-umbra`, dispatched by the Entire CLI\n  kubectl style. Its own Go module under `umbra/`.\n- Inputs come only through documented Entire and Graph output. No scraping of\n  internal state, no undocumented files.\n- Four boundaries behind interfaces, and exactly one Runner for external\n  processes, so tests replay recorded fixtures.\n- **No model anywhere in Umbra.** The core is deterministic and offline.\n- Four states: lit, penumbra, umbra, unknown, with five penumbra tiers.\n- Missing data is a state, never an error. A transcript with no tool records\n  gives every node `unknown`, which is the correct answer rather than a guess.\n- **Umbra never executes commands from a transcript.** Test ids are validated\n  against a strict pattern and passed as separate argv elements. There is no\n  `sh -c` anywhere in it.\n- Layout is computed in Go and written into the report JSON. The browser never\n  computes positions, only styles and states.\n- Vanilla JavaScript and CSS for the report and the site. No libraries, no\n  fonts fetched, no network requests, no motion on load in the report.\n- No em dashes in any file, code comments included.\n- Tests replay recorded fixtures. No test may need a live agent or a network.\n- `go test ./...` green at every commit. Commit after every phase, never squash.\n- Touch nothing outside `umbra/` except a one line pointer in the repository\n  README.\n- Run `entire graph impact` before changing a file the build did not create.\n- Keep the machine light: one agent session, no parallel builds, no background\n  processes left running.\n\n## What the reviewer is meant to get\n\nAn eclipse map that can be replayed in the order the agent looked at things,\nplus a one page packet a reviewer reads in a minute, plus an exit code a CI job\ncan act on.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2572,"cache_read_input_tokens":778595,"output_tokens":1348,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":308},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1348,"cache_read_input_tokens":778595,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2572},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CemZfdSLqjx6AvgNgBU6J","type":"assistant","uuid":"8d0f16a1-1a7c-4ab7-8ee0-46b53dc79664","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:35:48.943Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"8d0f16a1-1a7c-4ab7-8ee0-46b53dc79664","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"47ecdd8a-ca00-4576-a9bb-909e9e5db54c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UDeavWPQT74q7ap7Jrot8j","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/utkuputku/entire-graph/umbra/KICKOFF_PROMPT.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"2d87a7fd-eaaf-48e1-8773-fd6f5b14336a","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:35:51.534Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/utkuputku/entire-graph/umbra/KICKOFF_PROMPT.md","content":"# Kickoff prompt\n\nThis is the brief Umbra was built from, recorded here because the build never\nkept it as a file. It is reconstructed from the session record rather than\ncopied from an existing document, and it is placed in the first commit so the\nintent is in the repository before any code is.\n\n## The problem\n\nFind the code an AI agent's change affects but the agent never looked at.\n\nA clean diff and a confident description tell a reviewer what changed. They do\nnot tell the reviewer what the agent never opened. Umbra takes the dependents of\nevery changed symbol from Entire Graph, subtracts what the session actually\nexamined according to the checkpoint's tool activity and the agent's own words,\nranks what is left in shadow, runs the tests that reach it, and then sweeps the\nwhole suite once so the selection audits itself.\n\n## Settled decisions, not open questions\n\n- Go, one static binary named `entire-umbra`, dispatched by the Entire CLI\n  kubectl style. Its own Go module under `umbra/`.\n- Inputs come only through documented Entire and Graph output. No scraping of\n  internal state, no undocumented files.\n- Four boundaries behind interfaces, and exactly one Runner for external\n  processes, so tests replay recorded fixtures.\n- **No model anywhere in Umbra.** The core is deterministic and offline.\n- Four states: lit, penumbra, umbra, unknown, with five penumbra tiers.\n- Missing data is a state, never an error. A transcript with no tool records\n  gives every node `unknown`, which is the correct answer rather than a guess.\n- **Umbra never executes commands from a transcript.** Test ids are validated\n  against a strict pattern and passed as separate argv elements. There is no\n  `sh -c` anywhere in it.\n- Layout is computed in Go and written into the report JSON. The browser never\n  computes positions, only styles and states.\n- Vanilla JavaScript and CSS for the report and the site. No libraries, no\n  fonts fetched, no network requests, no motion on load in the report.\n- No em dashes in any file, code comments included.\n- Tests replay recorded fixtures. No test may need a live agent or a network.\n- `go test ./...` green at every commit. Commit after every phase, never squash.\n- Touch nothing outside `umbra/` except a one line pointer in the repository\n  README.\n- Run `entire graph impact` before changing a file the build did not create.\n- Keep the machine light: one agent session, no parallel builds, no background\n  processes left running.\n\n## What the reviewer is meant to get\n\nAn eclipse map that can be replayed in the order the agent looked at things,\nplus a one page packet a reviewer reads in a minute, plus an exit code a CI job\ncan act on.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8d0f16a1-1a7c-4ab7-8ee0-46b53dc79664","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"2d87a7fd-eaaf-48e1-8773-fd6f5b14336a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14985792 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"17abfac6-b1b4-4c30-b255-9c412c4428c2","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:35:51.647Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"50c05c30-88dc-4199-9bfd-3e509ccd25d4","snapshotMessageId":"221df550-e472-44fd-95f3-bd3bf7438f13","trackingPath":"/home/utkuputku/entire-graph/umbra/HANDOFF.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-09-06T04:36:11.476Z","realParentDir":"/home/utkuputku/entire-graph/umbra"},"timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:36:11.476Z"}
{"parentUuid":"17abfac6-b1b4-4c30-b255-9c412c4428c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemZhYxGwNdq2yeA18ruR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DJJxMbULd6DHD9UpJy4xY2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/utkuputku/entire-graph/umbra/HANDOFF.md","content":"# Handoff\n\nWritten at graft time, on the day Umbra was moved into this fork. It is not a\ndocument that existed during the build, and it does not pretend to be one.\nWhat follows is the state of the work being handed over.\n\n## What is being handed over\n\nUmbra, a plugin for the Entire CLI, run as `entire umbra <checkpoint>`. It\nlives in `umbra/` as its own Go module and imports no package from\n`entire-graph`. The upstream repository is untouched apart from this directory\nand the agent files `entire graph init-agents` writes.\n\n## Where it came from\n\nThe work was built in a separate repository over nineteen phases, each one a\ncommit with its test count in the message, with `go test ./...` green at every\none. That repository's history and its checkpoint trail are not carried across.\nThis fork's trail begins here, at the graft, and the first two commits say so:\none for the planning documents, one for the import of the code as a single\nclearly labelled commit.\n\nThe reason for the split is stated plainly rather than left to be noticed. The\noriginal repository's checkpoint refs hold whole session transcripts, including\nmaterial from an unrelated project that happened to be read in the first\nminutes of the build. None of it is pushed here. This mirror starts clean and\nstays clean.\n\n## State at handoff\n\n- 320 tests green across nine packages.\n- The demo run against the seeded fixture reports 8 probes selected, 5 cracked,\n  a full sweep and 0 leaks.\n- The report renders as a self contained HTML file with no external requests,\n  and the site renders from `file://`.\n- `entire graph doctor --json` reports `no_egress: true`.\n\n## What is not done\n\n- `umbra clean` is described in `docs/SECURITY_AND_ACCESS.md` and was never\n  built. Worktrees are deleted by hand.\n- The examined set is built from tool activity, so an agent that reads and\n  edits through the shell leaves little trace and its work looks unexamined.\n  Umbra found this in its own build and it is disclosed rather than tuned away.\n- A worktree left behind by a different live checkout of the same repository is\n  still reused, which can fail a run that did nothing wrong.\n\n## What the next person should read first\n\n`docs/PRD.md` for what it is for, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for how it is put\ntogether, then `NOTES.md` for what the build found and where those two\ndocuments turned out to be wrong about the installed tools.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1434,"cache_read_input_tokens":781167,"output_tokens":884,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1434,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":781167,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1434},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CemZhQ8x547ZrDLXtEjJz","type":"assistant","uuid":"50c05c30-88dc-4199-9bfd-3e509ccd25d4","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:36:09.453Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
