{"parentUuid":"b28e0e3a-cafe-4e65-accf-f1e38b465e59","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemZjrS3ytqbtX2fMVzhU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Exactly six files staged, no product code. Let me pull the rejected options from NOTES so the checkpoint carries real reasoning."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":783565,"output_tokens":757,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":501},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":561,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":783565,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":561},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CemZji1YVz2Mz658SL2jW","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d327901-2ae1-4dd7-938d-a4d677e99161","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:36:36.088Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"2d327901-2ae1-4dd7-938d-a4d677e99161","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemZjrS3ytqbtX2fMVzhU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BojeUarMpFEvvJVotZosqg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra/umbra\nsed -n '/^## Deviations from the letter of the plan, and why/,/^## Phases 6 to 11/p' NOTES.md | head -20\necho \"=== ============================= ===\"\nsed -n '/^## Honest limits of this particular demo/,/^## Deviations/p' NOTES.md | head -14","description":"Read the rejected options and deviations from NOTES"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":783565,"output_tokens":757,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":501},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":561,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":757,"cache_read_input_tokens":783565,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":561},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CemZji1YVz2Mz658SL2jW","type":"assistant","uuid":"f55ed21c-20f0-47e6-81a5-cfc9d3215fac","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:36:38.006Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"f55ed21c-20f0-47e6-81a5-cfc9d3215fac","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"47ecdd8a-ca00-4576-a9bb-909e9e5db54c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BojeUarMpFEvvJVotZosqg","type":"tool_result","content":"## Deviations from the letter of the plan, and why\n\n- `fixtures/app` had four modules and four pytest files as the kickoff\n  specifies. Phase 13 added a fifth of each, `app/report.py` and\n  `tests/test_report.py`, because the `leak` scenario in ARCHITECTURE.md needs\n  a chain four hops long through `render_lines` and the kickoff's inventory did\n  not contain one. See the phase 13 section below.\n- Before editing `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, which is a file this build did not\n  create, `entire graph impact --symbol Open-questions --repo .` was run as the\n  rules require. It answered `IMPACT DEGENERATE: Open-questions has no callers,\n  callees or type consumers`, which is expected for a Markdown section, so the\n  edit was safe.\n\n## Phases 6 to 11\n=== ============================= ===\n## Honest limits of this particular demo\n\nThe exposure comes from the checkpoint of the session that built Umbra, which\nis one long session covering the whole build rather than a short session that\nends at the commit. Two consequences show in the output above:\n\n- The session-said line falls back to the last thing the agent said, which is a\n  sentence of narration rather than a commit summary. In a short session ending\n  at a commit it would be the closing account of the change. The fallback is\n  bounded by the last edit to a source file where it can be, and the header\n  always names where the sentence came from.\n- Files touched anywhere in the long session are lit for every commit in it, so\n  the illumination fraction is not comparable to a short session's.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6cb011ec-8ebc-4b52-97de-7a1f08e6c509","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:36:40.729Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Deviations from the letter of the plan, and why\n\n- `fixtures/app` had four modules and four pytest files as the kickoff\n  specifies. Phase 13 added a fifth of each, `app/report.py` and\n  `tests/test_report.py`, because the `leak` scenario in ARCHITECTURE.md needs\n  a chain four hops long through `render_lines` and the kickoff's inventory did\n  not contain one. See the phase 13 section below.\n- Before editing `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, which is a file this build did not\n  create, `entire graph impact --symbol Open-questions --repo .` was run as the\n  rules require. It answered `IMPACT DEGENERATE: Open-questions has no callers,\n  callees or type consumers`, which is expected for a Markdown section, so the\n  edit was safe.\n\n## Phases 6 to 11\n=== ============================= ===\n## Honest limits of this particular demo\n\nThe exposure comes from the checkpoint of the session that built Umbra, which\nis one long session covering the whole build rather than a short session that\nends at the commit. Two consequences show in the output above:\n\n- The session-said line falls back to the last thing the agent said, which is a\n  sentence of narration rather than a commit summary. In a short session ending\n  at a commit it would be the closing account of the change. The fallback is\n  bounded by the last edit to a source file where it can be, and the header\n  always names where the sentence came from.\n- Files touched anywhere in the long session are lit for every commit in it, so\n  the illumination fraction is not comparable to a short session's.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f55ed21c-20f0-47e6-81a5-cfc9d3215fac","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra/umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
