{"parentUuid":"9a23f55c-f9bb-4718-879b-ab7b6ace7856","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemZmn89ZzWpLavDJ1VdC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the reasoning material. Making the first commit."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":785430,"output_tokens":1593,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":72},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":676,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1593,"cache_read_input_tokens":785430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":676},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CemZmcirTvYmtJCnCvi4c","type":"assistant","uuid":"51ae0831-2f5e-43a5-9ac2-ac8d7b67751f","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:36:55.557Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"51ae0831-2f5e-43a5-9ac2-ac8d7b67751f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemZmn89ZzWpLavDJ1VdC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DMGdg7ydTCCHqUe9ZgCc7i","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"$HOME/entire-graph\"\ngit -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\numbra: initial understanding and intended architecture\n\nThe planning documents and the brief, committed before any product code, so\nthe intent is in this repository ahead of the implementation.\n\nWHAT UMBRA IS\n\nUmbra finds the code an AI agent's change affects but the agent never looked\nat. A clean diff and a confident description tell a reviewer what changed.\nThey do not tell the reviewer what the agent never opened.\n\nWHY THE SUBTRACTION IS THE PRODUCT\n\nThe blast radius on its own is not new: Entire Graph already answers what a\nchange reaches. Attention on its own is not useful: a list of files an agent\nread says nothing about risk. The product is the subtraction. Take every\ndependent of every changed symbol from Graph, subtract what the session\nactually examined according to the checkpoint's tool activity and the agent's\nown words, and rank what is left. That difference is the thing a reviewer\ncannot get any other way, and it is the only reason this tool needs both\nGraph and Checkpoints rather than either alone.\n\nTHE FOUR STATES\n\n  lit       read with a range covering the symbol, at or after the change\n            began, or edited\n  penumbra  half seen, in five tiers: glance, a partial read whose range\n            missed the symbol; glimpse, only a search hit on the file;\n            quoted, its content appeared inside a tool result; afterimage,\n            read fully but only before the change began; echo, named in the\n            agent's own words and never opened\n  umbra     nothing in the session touched the file or named it\n  unknown   the transcript carries no tool events and no mentions\n\nMissing data is a state, never an error. A transcript with no tool records\ngives every node unknown, which is the correct answer rather than a guess,\nand the selection falls back to the graph alone.\n\nSETTLED DECISIONS\n\nGo, one static binary, its own module under umbra/, importing no package from\nentire-graph. Inputs only through documented Entire and Graph output. Four\nboundaries behind interfaces and exactly one Runner, so tests replay recorded\nfixtures and no test needs a live agent or a network. Layout computed in Go\nand written into the report JSON, so the browser never computes positions.\nVanilla JavaScript and CSS, no libraries, no fonts fetched, no requests.\n\nTwo rules are security decisions rather than preferences. There is no model\nanywhere in Umbra, so the core is deterministic and offline. And Umbra never\nexecutes a command from a transcript: test ids are validated against a strict\npattern and passed as separate argv elements, and there is no sh -c in it.\n\nWHAT WAS CONSIDERED AND REJECTED\n\nAdapters for other agents, because a transcript with no tool records already\ngets unknown, which is correct. Subagent transcripts. Live mode during a\nsession and a blind spot budget gate, because shadow branch data is not\ndocumented output and this build takes nothing undocumented. Mutability\nanalysis of callees, because nothing in the documented surface provides it.\nCoverage deltas, which need coverage tooling in the target repository. Trend\ndashboards. Cross repository dependents.\n\nAnd the largest one: Umbra never writes code. It shows the shadow, it does\nnot fix it. A tool that both finds the unexamined and edits it is a tool\nwhose findings nobody can check.\n\nWHAT THE PROBE CONFIRMED BEFORE ANY OF THIS WAS BUILT\n\nRead inputs carry offset and limit for a partial read and neither for a full\none, so the glance tier is real rather than assumed. graph impact reports\nexact call site lines, so the fault line and beacon factors are live and the\nranker keeps all six. graph commit distinguishes a signature change from a\nbody change and carries dependent counts, so the source weights stand. graph\nverify names newly failing tests against a recorded baseline, which is what\nmakes a cracked probe distinguishable from a test that was already red.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gqxi2oeEAPrkQtZqBPR6dP\nMSG\necho \"commit exit: $?\"\ngit log --oneline -1 | cat\necho \"=== files in this commit ===\"\ngit show --stat --oneline HEAD | head -10","description":"Make the first commit with real reasoning"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":785430,"output_tokens":1593,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":72},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":676,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1593,"cache_read_input_tokens":785430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":676},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CemZmcirTvYmtJCnCvi4c","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd472237-b9b7-4b28-aa84-89921b6f92ce","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:37:13.468Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
