{"parentUuid":"28bd6f53-930f-427d-a51a-330d417819eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cemb487zGRmwBj95ygKJ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":831000,"output_tokens":2602,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":740},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":2602,"cache_read_input_tokens":831000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cemb3uZC2QPp4Wozwbhz5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a2586c1-b552-41a9-a83e-5333eb032179","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:53:53.391Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"3a2586c1-b552-41a9-a83e-5333eb032179","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cemb487zGRmwBj95ygKJ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Status report while the demo run finishes.\n\n## 1. Mirror and plugin: both working, yes\n\n**Mirror.** Fork `u7k4rs6/entire-graph` created. Mirror registered on **`aws-ap-south-1`, jurisdiction `in`** and reported `ready`. I didn't need the picker: `entire api /api/v1/clusters` enumerated the regions, so I named the repo and the India cluster explicitly as arguments. Cloned to `~/entire-graph` (under `$HOME`, not scratch).\n\nThe clone is clean, verified: **zero `refs/entire/*`**. `entire status` reports `Enabled · branch main`, `Checkpoints sync to: origin`, and origin is `entire://aws-ap-south-1.entire.io/gh/u7k4rs6/entire-graph`. No `entire configure --checkpoint-remote` was run at all.\n\n**Plugin.** Built from source with CGO in about 90 seconds, no fallback to the release archive needed. `entire graph version` → `dev`. `init-agents` wrote `.entire/graph-agent.md` and updated `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n`entire graph doctor --json` recorded: **`no_egress: true`**, every `phase_1_local_only` flag false, every `features_requiring_network_access` false. You were right that this beats inferring it from capabilities.\n\n## 2. Relations: `full` is the default, and all five are present\n\nDefault profile is **`full`** on both `snapshot` and `impact`, and Umbra passes no `--profile` anywhere. Under `fast` only CALLS survives, so this mattered.\n\nI didn't stop at the table. A real snapshot emits, repo-wide / fixture app: CALLS 1856/29, DATA_FLOWS 441/11, USES_TYPE 281/9, FILE_CHANGES_WITH 162/1, TESTS 11/2. **No degradation, no flag needed.**\n\nOne trap: Python's per-language list omits TESTS and FILE_CHANGES_WITH. Those are listed for **0 of 185 languages** because they're derived, not parsed. Expected, not a degradation. Also worth knowing: `graph search` defaults to `fast`, unlike snapshot and impact.\n\n## 3. Demo numbers\n\n**In the source repo, with this newly built plugin: 8 probes selected, 5 cracked, full sweep, 0 leaks.** Exact match.\n\n**In the fork, the fixture demo cannot be reproduced by reference, and I know why.** Four end-to-end tests skip with:\n\n```\n\"0063443\" is neither a checkpoint nor a commit: git rev-parse 0063443 exited 128\n```\n\n`0063443` is the seeded fixture change in the source repository's history, which was deliberately not carried across. The `entire umbra HEAD` run is still going (HEAD is the import commit, which adds 200+ files at once, so `graph commit` is slow) and will not produce 8/5/0/0 either, because it isn't that change.\n\nTo reproduce the claim here, the seeded signature change needs replaying as a commit in this repo. That's honest and I can do it. Say the word and I will.\n\n## 4. Graph evidence recorded\n\nTwo of three, written into BUILDATHON.md with verification:\n\n- **Relations** as above, documentation read then measured.\n- **`graph search`** for where the umbra/penumbra decision is made returned **LOW CONFIDENCE**, flagged its top two ranks as tied, and pointed at `appendPenumbra` in `umbra.js`, which *draws* a penumbra and decides nothing. Verified against source: the decision is `ClassifyAt` at `classify.go:35`, confirmed by `graph def` and pinned by `jsmirror_test.go:122`. The tool was honest about its uncertainty and the warning was correct.\n\nNot yet done: the final `graph diff`, and the impact-analysis-before-a-change.\n\n## 5. BUILDATHON.md sections still empty\n\nWritten: name, summary, problem and user, track and why Entire is essential, architecture and workflow, findings 1 and 2, setup/run/test, and all four required limitations.\n\nEmpty: **Noon Curveball** (as instructed), **Finding 3** (the semantic diff), and **Checkpoints**.\n\n## Two things needing your decision\n\n**Checkpoints are blocked, and I won't work around it the wrong way.** There is no `entire checkpoint create`. Checkpoints come from agent hooks during a session, and `entire session attach` links a session's transcript to the last commit. This Claude Code session runs with its working directory in the *old* repo, so no transcript exists under the new clone and nothing fired for my two commits. I could attach the old build session, and I deliberately have not: **that would copy its transcript, including the unrelated project's material, straight into the clean mirror.** The clean fix is to run Claude Code from `~/entire-graph` so hooks fire naturally. That's your call.\n\n**Both commits are local; nothing has been pushed.** `d25e5b51` (the four planning documents plus HANDOFF.md and KICKOFF_PROMPT.md, no product code) and `42f215f8` (the import, 207 files, labelled as an import rather than a fabricated history). Tests green: 315 pass, 4 skip for the `0063443` reason above.\n\nI also wrote HANDOFF.md and KICKOFF_PROMPT.md rather than leave Step 4 short, since neither existed. Both say plainly at the top that they were written at graft time and are not documents that existed during the build."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":831000,"output_tokens":2602,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":740},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":2602,"cache_read_input_tokens":831000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cemb3uZC2QPp4Wozwbhz5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c9b14fe5-406f-4180-89fb-3ac66695f5ca","timestamp":"2026-09-06T04:54:16.624Z","