{"parentUuid":"b04f69d1-74e6-4949-870e-818074cc3cea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cemc2T26WmqjtoKzDR52P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ABHqmUXR5heodZU9T9hvwh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"$HOME/entire-graph/umbra\"\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/share/mise/installs/go/1.26.3/bin:$PATH\"\ngo test -count=1 ./... 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(FAIL|ok)\" | grep FAIL || echo \"all packages green\"\ncd \"$HOME/entire-graph\"\ngit add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\numbra: BUILDATHON.md, and restore a deny rule the graft dropped\n\nThe semantic diff of the graft found something worth the whole exercise.\n\nentire graph diff --base d25e5b51 --head HEAD reports 2331 entities added,\n2 changed and 2 removed. The two removals were the first two lines of output:\n\n  .claude/settings.json (JSON)\n    - section permissions removed (10 dependents)\n    - section deny removed (12 dependents)\n\nVerified against upstream. Commit 3a2a715f, which this fork branches from,\ncarries a permissions.deny rule blocking Read(./.entire/metadata/**). It is\nupstream's own rule and nothing here intended to touch it. It was removed as a\nside effect of running entire enable -y --agent claude-code in step 1, which\nrewrites that file to install its hooks.\n\nRestored, with the hooks that enable legitimately added kept, both read back\nout of the file to confirm.\n\nA plain git diff would have shown those five lines somewhere inside a 207 file\ncommit, and nobody reads 207 files. The semantic diff ranked a two line\nremoval above 2331 additions because removals with dependents are what break\nthings. That is Graph driving a decision rather than confirming one, and the\ndecision went against my own work.\n\nBUILDATHON.md carries the participant guide's outline with four findings, each\nwritten with how it was verified against source and tests rather than as a\nfact: the relation profiles measured rather than inferred, a graph search that\ndeclared low confidence and was right to, why the demo numbers do not\nreproduce in this clone, and this diff. The Noon Curveball section is\ndeliberately empty. The checkpoint section points at the limitation that this\nrepository has no checkpoints of its own yet.\n\nThe diff also ends with E_PARSE_ERROR warnings on upstream's vendored\ntree-sitter grammar headers, saying dependent references there may be\nundercounted. That is recorded rather than dropped, so the dependent counts\nabove read as approximate.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gqxi2oeEAPrkQtZqBPR6dP\nMSG\necho \"commit exit: $?\"; git log --oneline -4 | cat","description":"Verify tests and commit BUILDATHON plus the fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1632,"cache_read_input_tokens":846487,"output_tokens":968,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1632,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":968,"cache_read_input_tokens":846487,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1632},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cemc2Jm1MKtMB4BsRKvRC","type":"assistant","uuid":"e63ab4e3-f24e-4d26-af95-40768912b411","timestamp":"2026-09-06T05:06:40.430Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"e63ab4e3-f24e-4d26-af95-40768912b411","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6528d5de-42eb-4f31-b553-7bfb27d63234","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ABHqmUXR5heodZU9T9hvwh","type":"tool_result","content":"all packages green\ncommit exit: 0\n57cea764 umbra: BUILDATHON.md, and restore a deny rule the graft dropped\n42f215f8 umbra: import the plugin as one commit\nd25e5b51 umbra: initial understanding and intended architecture\n3a2a715f Merge pull request #211 from entireio/paulo-perf\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"65d2b0d6-75fb-4fc2-af3e-691ce87f67ab","timestamp":"2026-09-06T05:06:48.263Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"all packages green\ncommit exit: 0\n57cea764 umbra: BUILDATHON.md, and restore a deny rule the graft dropped\n42f215f8 umbra: import the plugin as one commit\nd25e5b51 umbra: initial understanding and intended architecture\n3a2a715f Merge pull request #211 from entireio/paulo-perf","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e63ab4e3-f24e-4d26-af95-40768912b411","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"65d2b0d6-75fb-4fc2-af3e-691ce87f67ab","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14919220 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f13a3120-994b-4640-b25e-47cab217b4a8","timestamp":"2026-09-06T05:06:48.294Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"f13a3120-994b-4640-b25e-47cab217b4a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cemc4R8J9dh9NGMQbErtq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three commits in, tests green. Here's where Steps 1 through 7 stand.\n\n## Mirror and plugin: both working\n\n- **Fork:** `u7k4rs6/entire-graph`, confirmed a fork of `entireio/entire-graph`.\n- **Mirror:** `aws-ap-south-1`, jurisdiction `in`, status `ready`. I skipped the picker: `entire api /api/v1/clusters` enumerated the regions, so I named the repo and the India cluster as explicit arguments.\n- **Clone:** `~/entire-graph`, under `$HOME`. **Zero `refs/entire/*`** — clean, verified. `entire status` reports checkpoints syncing to `origin`, which is the India mirror. No `--checkpoint-remote` was ever run.\n- **Plugin:** built from source with CGO, no fallback needed. `entire graph version` → `dev`. `doctor` records **`no_egress: true`**.\n\n## Relations\n\nDefault profile is **`full`** on both `snapshot` and `impact`; Umbra passes no `--profile`. Measured on a real snapshot rather than inferred — repo / fixture: CALLS 1856/29, DATA_FLOWS 441/11, USES_TYPE 281/9, FILE_CHANGES_WITH 162/1, TESTS 11/2. **All five present, no degradation.** Python's per-language list omits TESTS and FILE_CHANGES_WITH because those are listed for 0 of 185 languages — derived, not parsed.\n\n## Demo numbers\n\n**Source repo: 8 selected, 5 cracked, full sweep, 0 leaks.** Exact match with the new plugin.\n\n**This clone: does not reproduce, and I found out why.** `0063443` is the seeded fixture commit from the source history, deliberately not carried across; four e2e tests say so rather than failing quietly. `entire umbra HEAD` doesn't substitute: my graft commits carry no checkpoint trailer, so Umbra fell back to pairing by session window and began reading one of upstream's 94 inherited checkpoints — one is 3.4M tokens, which is why it blew its timeout. Written up in BUILDATHON.md, not papered over.\n\n## Graph evidence: four findings recorded\n\nThe fourth is the one that earned its keep. The semantic diff reported 2331 entities added, 2 changed, **2 removed** — and the two removals were the first lines of output:\n\n```\n.claude/settings.json (JSON)\n  - section permissions removed (10 dependents)\n  - section deny removed (12 dependents)\n```\n\nVerified against `3a2a715f`: upstream carries a `permissions.deny` rule blocking `Read(./.entire/metadata/**)`. **`entire enable -y --agent claude-code` stripped it** when it rewrote that file to install hooks. Nothing intended that. Restored, hooks kept, both read back to confirm.\n\nA plain `git diff` would have buried those five lines inside a 207-file commit. The semantic diff ranked a two-line removal above 2331 additions because removals with dependents are what break things. It's also a finding against my own work rather than a flattering one.\n\n## BUILDATHON.md sections still empty\n\n- **Noon Curveball** — deliberately, as instructed.\n- **Checkpoints and what each proves** — blocked, see below.\n\nEverything else is written: summary, problem and user, track and why Entire is essential, architecture and workflow, four findings with verification, setup/run/test, and all four required limitations including the shell-driven-agent blind spot, the stale worktree with deletion paths, `umbra clean` being documented but unbuilt, and checks only being trusted once observed failing.\n\n## The one thing I need from you\n\n**Checkpoints cannot be created from where I'm sitting.** There is no `entire checkpoint create`; they come from agent hooks during a session. This session's working directory is the old repo, so nothing fired for my three commits. `entire session attach` would work, but the only transcript available is the old build session — and attaching it would copy that transcript, including the unrelated project's material, straight into the clean mirror. I won't do that.\n\nThe fix is to run Claude Code from `~/entire-graph` so hooks fire naturally. Step 8 and Step 10 both depend on it, and it also unblocks a meaningful demo run here.\n\nNothing has been pushed yet. Three commits local: `d25e5b51` (docs only), `42f215f8` (import, 207 files), `57cea764` (BUILDATHON.md plus the deny-rule restore)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1142,"cache_read_input_tokens":848119,"output_tokens":1516,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1142,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1516,"cache_read_input_tokens":848119,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1142,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1142},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cemc4EeWiCPjw5t7MMRb3","type":"assistant","uuid":"be0a9090-06d2-48aa-b872-c7e5bf2b2940","timestamp":"2026-09-06T05:07:11.867Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
