{"parentUuid":"96c63b5a-1b2f-4aac-9cbd-628bd65d6c09","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"Goal is grafting Umbra into your entire-graph fork for the buildathon. Mirror, plugin and three commits are done locally, and BUILDATHON.md is written apart from the Curveball. Next: open Claude Code from ~/entire-graph so checkpoint hooks fire. (disable recaps in /config)","timestamp":"2026-09-06T05:10:21.162Z","uuid":"f253bd2d-6cda-41a6-882a-530ff501b83d","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"f253bd2d-6cda-41a6-882a-530ff501b83d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"73f148b9-9eb5-460c-be2e-7a5a03ef40f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are in ~/entire-graph on branch umbra-buildathon, hooks live, tree clean.\nRead umbra/NOTES.md and umbra/BUILDATHON.md first. An external review found ten\nissues. You are fixing two of them in code, correcting the docs, and recording\nthe rest honestly. Do NOT attempt the other issues; time is short and a rushed\nfix to test selection is worse than a documented gap.\n\nNo em dashes. go test ./... green before every commit. Commit each of the four\ntasks separately with an Entire-Checkpoint trailer. Stop by 14:15 IST regardless\nof where you are, so the tree is clean and pushed before submission.\n\n1. The sweep must never report a false zero. umbra/cmd/entire-umbra/execute.go:99\n   When verification is degraded and emits no test IDs, the leak count is\n   currently reported as 0, which is indistinguishable from a real clean sweep.\n   Change it so a sweep with no comparable test IDs reports \"audit inconclusive\"\n   with the reason, in the terminal, JSON, HTML and packet, and never the number\n   zero. A real sweep that compares IDs and finds nothing still reports 0 leaks.\n   Add a known-positive test: force the degraded path and assert the output says\n   inconclusive and contains no zero-leak claim. Confirm the test fails if you\n   revert the fix.\n\n2. A failed read must not mark a node lit.\n   umbra/internal/transcript/claudecode.go:125 and :137\n   The parser records a Read before the result arrives and ignores\n   tool_result.is_error, so a failed file read counts as inspected. Pair each\n   tool_use with its tool_result and drop any read whose result is an error.\n   This can only ever move nodes toward shadow, never away from it, so verify the\n   demo numbers after: rerun the demo commit and confirm 8 selected, 5 cracked,\n   0 leaks still holds, and report any change in the state counts.\n   Add a fixture with one successful read and one errored read, and assert only\n   the successful one lands in the examined set. Confirm it fails without the fix.\n\n3. Sync the documentation to what exists.\n   umbra/docs/SECURITY_AND_ACCESS.md:25 and anywhere else claiming behavior the\n   binary does not have: .umbra.json, umbra clean, --scrub, and Graph timeout\n   behavior. The four planning documents stay as written per the standing rule,\n   so do NOT edit them to hide the gap: instead add a short, clearly headed\n   section to the README listing every command and flag the design documents\n   describe that was never built, with the manual alternative where one exists.\n   Also scope the Go claim: state plainly that test selection and execution are\n   supported for Python via pytest, and that Go test selection is not yet\n   working, since a Go test ID is passed in a form go test reads as a package\n   rather than as -run.\n   Also handle --adapter, which is accepted but ignored while the output always\n   claims Claude Code: either reject an unsupported value with a clear message,\n   or document it as accepted-but-unused. Prefer rejecting.\n\n4. Write the review into BUILDATHON.md under known limitations, as its own short\n   section. List all ten findings in plain language, say which two you fixed and\n   why those two, and say why the rest are documented rather than patched under\n   time pressure. Include the observation that five of them passed go test and\n   go vet while asserting nothing about the behavior they name, which is the same\n   class of problem as the Box.Overlaps case already recorded in NOTES.md.\n   Do not soften the findings and do not claim anything is fixed that is not.\n\nThen: push, confirm the branch is up to date, and report with the demo numbers\nafter fix 2, the two known-positive tests and proof each fails without its fix,\nthe final test count, and the commit SHA to submit."},"uuid":"8e0abbda-f04a-4a66-89b7-019ca726a68c","timestamp":"2026-09-06T06:19:12.396Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
