{"parentUuid":"7cd52783-4840-4146-9119-e35564c06539","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"73f148b9-9eb5-460c-be2e-7a5a03ef40f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018UkmVZAigjo2yX8fRa58N8","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task 3 recon: what the docs claim vs what exists ===\n--- .umbra.json ---\ndocs/PRD.md:97:- Landing page that renders any `umbra.json` dropped onto it, client-side, with real examples from imported past sessions.\ndocs/SECURITY_AND_ACCESS.md:16:Umbra trusts Graph and CLI output as data, never as instructions. It trusts nothing inside a transcript. It trusts flags and a committed `.umbra.json`.\ndocs/SECURITY_AND_ACCESS.md:25:| The runner prefix is destructive or slow | Data loss or hang | The runner comes only from `--test` or a committed `.umbra.json`; Umbra echoes the full command before running; default timeout 10 minutes per invocation, and the default sweep (full suite) has its own 20 minute timeout after which the report says the sweep was cut short; everything runs in detached worktrees, never in the user's working tree |\ninternal/report/seal.go:60:\t// The runner prefix comes from a flag or from .umbra.json and is printed\n--- umbra clean ---\ndocs/SECURITY_AND_ACCESS.md:28:| Worktrees leak or fill the disk | Stale analysis, disk pressure | Keyed by sha under `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` or `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/umbra`; removed on exit unless `--keep-worktrees`; `umbra clean` removes all |\n--- --scrub ---\ndocs/SECURITY_AND_ACCESS.md:55:- Fixture recordings are scrubbed with `umbra record --scrub` and hand-reviewed before commit.\n--- --adapter ---\ncmd/entire-umbra/options.go:29:\tAdapter  string // auto, claude-code\ncmd/entire-umbra/options.go:85:func validAdapter(s string) bool {\ncmd/entire-umbra/options.go:104:\tif !validAdapter(o.Adapter) {\ncmd/entire-umbra/options.go:105:\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"--adapter must be auto or claude-code, not %q\", o.Adapter)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umb