{"parentUuid":"83783d9c-1e52-44ef-b4d5-318251e5892a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemiXrFMYutqWpsHQfiLA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FysXZsm5jxcXrhvRCRpqic","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/entire-graph\ngit -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\numbra: the sweep never reports a false zero\n\nThe sweep printed \"0 leaks\" whether it had compared every test in the suite\nand found nothing, or had compared nothing at all because the runner printed\nno per-test ids. Those are opposite findings and they read identically. It was\nthe strongest claim the report can make, made out of the weakest evidence it\nhas.\n\nWhen verify comes back degraded and produces no comparable ids, the sweep now\nsets SweepInconclusive with the reason and returns before computing leaks. No\nleak count is printed anywhere: not the terminal, not the JSON, not the HTML\nheader, not the packet. A sweep that did compare ids and found nothing still\nreports 0 leaks, because that is a real result.\n\nThe reason travels with the finding, so a reader is not left guessing:\n\"the runner printed no per-test ids, so the sweep could not compare any test\nagainst the baseline; add -v to the runner\". It goes through the scrubber like\nevery other string that reaches a report.\n\nKnown-positive, in internal/report/sweep_inconclusive_test.go. It renders all\nfour surfaces from an inconclusive analysis and asserts each says inconclusive\nand that none contains \"0 leaks\", \"0 leak\" or \"full sweep, 0\". A third test\nasserts the converse, that a genuinely clean sweep still says 0 leaks, so the\nfix cannot have traded one wrong answer for another.\n\nProved by reverting. With the three renderer branches disabled the test fails\non terminal, packet and HTML with exactly the claim the fix exists to prevent:\n  terminal: claims \"0 leaks\" from a sweep that compared nothing\n  packet:   claims \"**0 leaks**\" from a sweep that compared nothing\n  html:     claims \"full sweep, 0\" from a sweep that compared nothing\nRestored, it passes.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gqxi2oeEAPrkQtZqBPR6dP\nMSG\necho \"exit=$?\"\ngit log -1 --format='%h %s%n  Entire-Checkpoint: %(trailers:key=Entire-Checkpoint,valueonly)'","description":"Commit task 1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":944,"cache_read_input_tokens":894242,"output_tokens":940,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":90},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":944,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":940,"cache_read_input_tokens":894242,"cache_creation_input_tokens":944,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":944},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CemiXhhtxJR4J49FvgmmT","type":"assistant","uuid":"a3f6d0a5-fee7-40cc-a8cc-7360d1b6173c","timestamp":"2026-09-06T06:31:57.617Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
