{"parentUuid":"07c6d777-6893-4bdd-9f30-58cbae087a00","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14947842 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fd7049e2-3a44-47e1-8b7d-77d74bcb22f7","timestamp":"2026-09-06T06:33:56.044Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"fd7049e2-3a44-47e1-8b7d-77d74bcb22f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemihpTjK4gtJX9UXArsn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014AhZWn6EemiwJEtB7dpj58","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/entire-graph\ngit -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\numbra: document what the design describes and the binary does not do\n\nThe four planning documents in docs/ stay as written, per the standing rule of\nthis build. That means they describe behaviour the binary does not have, and\nthe honest fix is not to quietly edit the design until it matches the code.\n\numbra/README.md gains a section, \"Documented but not built\", listing each gap\nwith the manual alternative where one exists:\n\n  .umbra.json, a committed file supplying the runner prefix, described in\n  SECURITY_AND_ACCESS.md lines 16 and 25. Never implemented; use --test.\n\n  umbra clean, described at line 28 as removing all worktrees. No such\n  subcommand. Delete by hand from the plugin data directory or the cache.\n\n  umbra record --scrub, described at line 55. There is no --scrub flag.\n  Scrubbing is not optional and always runs, and the --no-scrub escape hatch\n  that once existed was removed on purpose.\n\n  A 60 second timeout on any single Graph call and a 30 second snapshot\n  warning. Not implemented per call. The timeouts that exist are the 10 minute\n  verify invocation and the 20 minute sweep.\n\nOne stale comment in internal/report/seal.go still told a reader the runner\nprefix could come from .umbra.json. Corrected, because a false claim in a code\ncomment is a false claim.\n\nLANGUAGE SCOPE, STATED PLAINLY\n\nTest selection and execution work for Python through pytest, which is the only\npath with end to end coverage. Go test selection does not work. A test id is\nbuilt as file + \"::\" + name in internal/shadow/select.go, which is pytest's\nform, and VerifyRequest.Command appends the ids to the runner as plain\narguments. For go test a non-flag argument is a package pattern rather than a\nfilter, so an id like internal/shadow/select_test.go::TestSelectTests is read\nas a package name and selects nothing. Making it work needs the id translated\ninto -run '^Name$' plus a package path, which is not done. Umbra still maps and\nranks shadow in a Go repository; it is the probe step that does not apply, so\nuse --run none there.\n\nON --adapter, THE REVIEW WAS WRONG\n\nThe review says --adapter is accepted but ignored. It is not accepted. It is\nvalidated at cmd/entire-umbra/options.go and an unsupported value is rejected,\nwhich is the behaviour the brief asked for and which already existed. Verified\nrather than assumed:\n\n  $ entire umbra HEAD --adapter codex --run none\n  umbra: --adapter must be auto or claude-code, not \"codex\"\n\nThe accurate residue is smaller and is documented instead: both accepted values\nresolve to the same adapter and the report's adapter field is set directly in\nanalyze.go, so the flag is validated and then not otherwise used. It cannot\nmislead, because an unsupported value never runs.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gqxi2oeEAPrkQtZqBPR6dP\nMSG\necho \"exit=$?\"; git log --oneline -3 | cat\ncat /tmp/claude-1000/-home-utkuputku-Desktop-Umbra/abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014/tasks/b8zgywjh3.output 2>&1 | tail -4","description":"Commit task 3 and check the demo"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":772,"cache_read_input_tokens":902371,"output_tokens":1227,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":772,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1227,"cache_read_input_tokens