{"parentUuid":"6b5abe42-a1a2-4833-991b-d2836df04033","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14934237 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b341ae2a-8077-435d-bcec-491009c19158","timestamp":"2026-09-06T06:37:59.939Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"b341ae2a-8077-435d-bcec-491009c19158","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cemj1k25bQc4Muqa8rmhD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pushed and clean, at 12:07 IST with time to spare.\n\n## Demo numbers after fix 2\n\n**8 probes selected, 5 cracked, full sweep, 0 leaks.** Holds exactly, naming both refund tests and the three service tests.\n\nState counts: **0 lit, 9 penumbra, 4 umbra, 0 unknown.** Nothing moved, and I can tell you why rather than just assert it: the coverage line reads **0 file reads, 0 edits, 0 searches, 33 shell commands**. That session had no reads at all, so fix 2 provably could not have changed these numbers. **The demo does not exercise fix 2.** Its evidence is the fixture test, not this run.\n\n## The two known-positive tests, and proof each fails without its fix\n\n**Fix 1** — `internal/report/sweep_inconclusive_test.go`. Renders all four surfaces from an inconclusive analysis. Reverted (three renderer branches disabled), it fails with exactly the claim the fix prevents:\n\n```\nterminal: claims \"0 leaks\" from a sweep that compared nothing\npacket:   claims \"**0 leaks**\" from a sweep that compared nothing\nhtml:     claims \"full sweep, 0\" from a sweep that compared nothing\n```\n\nA third test asserts the converse, that a genuinely clean sweep still says 0 leaks, so the fix can't have traded one wrong answer for another.\n\n**Fix 2** — `internal/transcript/failed_read_test.go` plus `testdata/failed-read.jsonl`, one successful read and one `is_error` read. Reverted (filter disabled), it fails:\n\n```\na read that returned is_error was kept as evidence of inspection:\n  {Seq:4 Kind:read Path:app/missing.py ToolID:bad1}\nexpected exactly one surviving read, got 2\napp/missing.py failed to read and must stay in shadow\n```\n\n## Final test count\n\n**320 pass, 5 skip, 0 fail** (325 total, up 5 — exactly my two known-positives). `go vet` silent.\n\n## SHA to submit\n\n```\ndfefa42e6443947bb1b1f9e752722f30241c171c\n```\n\nBranch `umbra-buildathon`, tree clean, local and remote identical.\n\n## Four things you should know\n\n**The Entire-Checkpoint trailers are missing on all four commits.** The hooks are installed, but `entire session current` reports no active session in that worktree — my session's working directory is the old repo, so `commit-msg` had nothing to stamp. The only `entire-graph` transcript on disk is `4c5862c2`, from the session that ended at 11:36, before I started. Attaching it would claim my commits came from that session, which is false, so I didn't. This needs a session run from `~/entire-graph` to fix properly.\n\n**`main` is a protected branch** and rejected the push. That's presumably why your brief named `umbra-buildathon`; I created it at HEAD and pushed there. It carries 11 commits ahead of `main`, 4 mine and 7 from earlier sessions.\n\n**The review is wrong about `--adapter`.** It already rejects unsupported values: `umbra: --adapter must be auto or claude-code, not \"codex\"`. I verified it rather than assuming, and documented the accurate, smaller residue instead: both accepted values resolve to the same adapter and the report's field is set directly in `analyze.go`, so the flag is validated then unused.\n\n**I could only substantiate eight of the ten findings.** The review document isn't in the repo and your brief enumerated eight specifically enough to act on. I listed those eight and said so in BUILDATHON.md rather than inventing two to reach a round number. If you have the reviewer's full list, those two belong in that section.\n\nOne more recorded rather than dismissed: `cmd/entire-umbra` failed once mid-session and passed both immediate reruns, with the failing run taking 86 seconds against 20 for the passes. That points at the worktree path rather than either fix, and it's written into BUILDATHON.md as not understood."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":916291,"output_tokens":1341,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1341,"cache_read_input_tokens":916291,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cemj1a81yBBiXJJXcx2fu","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ab2463b-7f48-4537-88dd-35af2b64e01b","timestamp":"2026-09-06T06:38:22.076Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
