{"parentUuid":"6c777d45-6f80-4b86-8cb7-d3b92dbeb917","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14998889 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"156b30fd-a235-44c1-885d-00feaf06aaaa","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:30:56.201Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"156b30fd-a235-44c1-885d-00feaf06aaaa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cemo3s3HWMjM1ZAxduntn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, you don't. The submission is self-contained on the public fork.\n\n**No submitted document links to it.** Every URL was rewritten during the graft. A judge can clone `u7k4rs6/entire-graph`, check out `umbra-buildathon`, and run the whole thing without ever touching the private repo.\n\n**Keeping it private is the correct call anyway**, not a workaround. Its checkpoint refs hold whole session transcripts including material from an unrelated project, which is precisely why the mirror was started clean. Making it public would publish someone else's unreleased work.\n\n**The disclosure is already in the submission**, in four places, so nothing is being concealed by the repo being private:\n\n- `HANDOFF.md`: built in a separate repository over nineteen phases, and that history and checkpoint trail are not carried across\n- `README.md`: built in a standalone repository and then grafted into this fork\n- `BUILDATHON.md`: the source history was deliberately not carried across\n\nThat last one matters most. The honest bit isn't the repo's visibility, it's that the docs say plainly the fork's history is two graft commits rather than a nineteen-phase build. That's already written down.\n\n## The one thing to be ready for\n\nA judge who reads that and asks \"so where's the nineteen phases of evidence?\" has a fair question, because the fork can't show it. Your answer is that `NOTES.md` carries the phase-by-phase record as prose, and if they want the underlying history you can add them as a collaborator on the private repo or walk them through it live. Don't make it public on the spot — the transcript problem is real.\n\n## Separate from this, still outstanding\n\nThe install command in `README.md:58` still says `@main`, and `main` has no `umbra/` directory. Anyone following the setup instructions gets a 404. That's the thing most likely to cost you with a judge who tries to run it, and it's a one-line fix to point at `umbra-buildathon`. Want me to do that now?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1337,"cache_read_input_tokens":929817,"output_tokens":631,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1337,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":631,"cache_read_input_tokens":929817,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1337,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1337},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cemo3ixMexneW1RYXtysy","type":"assistant","uuid":"87e6742d-df44-40a4-b38c-275a97d32587","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:31:10.431Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
