{"parentUuid":"e7fc80c2-eff9-49a0-8416-57ba5f330229","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemoQc6gqzV5qa8JdjDBB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SvXh5hC4gNq1pddo7p3U3z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/entire-graph\ngit add umbra/cmd/entire-umbra/analyze.go umbra/internal/graph/impact.go umbra/internal/graph/evidence_test.go umbra/internal/shadow/partial_scenario_test.go\ngit -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\numbra: only a severe warning promotes a dependent to needs verification\n\nAn info warning is not doubt, and treating it as doubt made the new tier\nworthless.\n\nW_DATA_FLOW_EVIDENCE_UNMERGED is the only in-scope warning this repository\nproduces. Its own text says the relation, its confidence and its reason are\nunaffected: it describes a merged evidence array on some DATA_FLOWS edges and\nnothing more. Promoting on it turned all thirteen dependents of the demo commit\ninto needs verification, so every node carried the same tier and the tier\ncarried no information at all. That is the crying wolf failure, and an honesty\nfeature that fires on everything is worse than not having one.\n\nImpact now separates InScopeSevere, the in-scope warnings the provider did not\nmark info, from the full InScopeWarnings list. Only the severe half promotes a\ndependent. An info warning is still reported in the header, so nothing is\nhidden from the reader; it just does not move a node.\n\nInScopeFailures is added alongside it, so the count of partial failures the\nprovider did not scope to another language is computed in one place rather than\nrecomputed at each call site.\n\ngo test ./... green.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gqxi2oeEAPrkQtZqBPR6dP\nMSG\necho \"exit=$?\"; git log --oneline -1 | cat; git status --short | head -3; echo \"(blank = clean)\"","description":"Commit the dirty tree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_us