{"parentUuid":"f9c0b770-a806-4d16-8d7d-ffce1f6a12f7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"87aba2de-de35-4ff1-9e3a-cbed7d26b95f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxtKDS7tZDsLaUxMSWJP76","type":"tool_result","content":"umbra: the plan for the noon curveball, with the impact analysis\n\nGraph is evidence, not an oracle. The plan for carrying resolution and\nconfidence through to the reader, written into NOTES.md before any code\nchanges, in the form of the Constraint-change playbook it extends.\n\nRecords what Umbra reads from Graph today and throws away: every relation's\nresolution and confidence, the seven relation types capabilities already names\nas heuristic and which relations.go parses into a field nothing reads, the\nsnapshot summary's warnings, partial_failures and degraded completeness, and\nthe malformed-record skip that turns a broken snapshot into a clean-looking\nempty one.\n\nIncludes the required impact analysis on the four graph-reader symbols about\nto change: LoadSnapshot, Field.Dependents, ParseImpactJSON and NewRelationMap.\nThe tool refused to disambiguate Dependents across eight definitions, which is\nitself the constraint arriving from the tool the phase is about.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEntire-Checkpoint: 819829c9754c\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b31b3425-f9d5-4c5f-b9f5-927621e66869","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:36:36.410Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"umbra: the plan for the noon curveball, with the impact analysis\n\nGraph is evidence, not an oracle. The plan for carrying resolution and\nconfidence through to the reader, written into NOTES.md before any code\nchanges, in the form of the Constraint-change playbook it extends.\n\nRecords what Umbra reads from Graph today and throws away: every relation's\nresolution and confidence, the seven relation types capabilities already names\nas heuristic and which relations.go parses into a field nothing reads, the\nsnapshot summary's warnings, partial_failures and degraded completeness, and\nthe malformed-record skip that turns a broken snapshot into a clean-looking\nempty one.\n\nIncludes the required impact analysis on the four graph-reader symbols about\nto change: LoadSnapshot, Field.Dependents, ParseImpactJSON and NewRelationMap.\nThe tool refused to disambiguate Dependents across eight definitions, which is\nitself the constraint arriving from the tool the phase is about.\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\nEntire-Checkpoint: 819829c9754c","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f9c0b770-a806-4d16-8d7d-ffce1f6a12f7","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
