{"parentUuid":"227f6545-1819-4015-949b-d696efd1cadf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemoVZFBYUUCk5wctFmXd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have it accurately. Writing the Curveball section."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":944425,"output_tokens":2194,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":545},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":2194,"cache_read_input_tokens":944425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CemoVRY5t2Qnf6v172RGq","type":"assistant","uuid":"113fc4dc-078f-4a69-bc84-a972919dfde6","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:36:57.986Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"113fc4dc-078f-4a69-bc84-a972919dfde6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemoVZFBYUUCk5wctFmXd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N2mPSqidEoD5Aio9WTFwjz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/entire-graph\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport io\np = \"BUILDATHON.md\"; s = io.open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nold = \"*To be filled at noon.*\"\nnew = '''**The constraint: Graph is evidence, not an oracle. Carry that through to the\nreader.**\n\nUmbra was treating every edge Graph returned as equally true. It read each\nrelation's type and discarded everything the provider said about how sure it\nwas: the `resolution` and `confidence` on every relation record, the seven\nrelation types `capabilities` already names as heuristic, the snapshot\nheader's warnings and `partial_failures`, its completeness level, and the\nmalformed records the loader was skipping in silence. A name-only guess and a\ncall the provider had resolved to a definition arrived in the field as the\nsame edge.\n\nThe worst of it was the silent skip. A snapshot the loader could not read\nproduced an empty field, and an empty field looked exactly like a clean\nreading of the repository. **That is the same shape as the false zero the\nexternal review found in the sweep**, arriving independently in a different\npart of the system: the strongest claim made out of the weakest evidence.\n\n### What was built\n\n**The loader keeps what it was throwing away.** Resolution, confidence and the\nper-relation warning codes are retained. The header line and the trailing\nsummary record are read for what the snapshot says about its own completeness.\nMalformed and unusable records are counted and reported rather than dropped.\n\n**The walk carries the weakest hop.** A path's resolution is that of its least\nresolved link, not its first, and the hop that made a path heuristic is named.\nResolution enters the path tie-break below depth and family, so it can change\nwhich path is quoted for a node and never which nodes are in the field.\n\n**Three tiers on every dependent, in all four surfaces.**\n\n| Tier | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| confirmed | every hop resolved to a definition |\n| heuristic | the attaching relation is one the provider derives rather than parses |\n| needs verification | reached through a heuristic link the reader cannot see, or emitted under a partial failure or a degraded snapshot |\n\nThis is a **fourth axis beside state, tier and score, not a fifth state**. The\nfour states say what the session saw; this says what the graph knows. The four\nstates are untouched and the six ranking factors are untouched: `Score` reads\nnone of these fields.\n\n**The header says when the field may be incomplete**, in the graph's own codes:\nthe completeness level with its parsed-file count, partial failures by code,\nwarnings by code, records the loader could not read, and any impact answer the\ngraph flagged for a changed symbol.\n\n### One correction made to our own work\n\nPromoting a dependent on *any* in-scope warning turned **all thirteen**\ndependents of the demo commit into \"needs verification\". Every node carried the\nsame tier, so the tier carried no information at all.\n\nThe cause was `W_DATA_FLOW_EVIDENCE_UNMERGED`, severity `info`, whose own text\nsays the relation, its confidence and its reason are unaffected. Only warnings\nthe provider does *not* mark `info` now promote a node. An info warning is\nstill reported in the header, so nothing is hidden; it just does not move a\nnode. An honesty feature that fires on everything is worse than not having one.\n\n### The fixture, and why it is the strongest part\n\n`fixtures/partial` is a small Python project built to contain analysis the\ngraph cannot complete, driven by a ninth recorded scenario. Its graph capture\nwas taken from a throwaway repository holding only that directory, so the\nsummary record describes the fixture and nothing else. **Every number asserted\nwas measured from real provider output before it was written down.**\n\n`dispatch.py` reaches the changed symbol three ways at runtime, through a\nhandler table, through `getattr` and through `importlib`, and the provider\ndraws no edge for any of them. The four tests that exercise those paths are\n**absent from the field entirely**. That is correct behaviour, and it is the\nconcrete demonstration of why the report has to say the field is a lower\nbound rather than a complete answer.\n\n`billing.py` produces a chain whose three tiers fall out of real resolutions\nwith nothing constructed for the test: `apply` import_resolved and confirmed,\n`quote` type_inferred and heuristic, `invoice` an exact hop through an\ninferred chain and so needs verification, as does the test that reaches it.'''\nassert old in s\nio.open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s.replace(old, new, 1))\nprint(\"curveball section written\")\nPY\ngrep -c \"—\" BUILDATHON.md; grep -n \"To be filled\" BUILDATHON.md || echo \"  no placeholders left\"","description":"Write the Curveball section"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_read_input_tokens":944425,"output_tokens":2194,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":545},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":2194,"cache_read_input_tokens":944425,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1652,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1652},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CemoVRY5t2Qnf6v172RGq","type":"assistant","uuid":"70e9016b-d438-45d4-93f1-71a012cd3628","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:37:15.733Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
