{"parentUuid":"71676283-1012-43f9-baa0-e7f24adc6d47","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemoiGC81bqMr7C6eT9Nc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XPz7ARpoQEoiomyGftds1v","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/entire-graph\nawk '/^## Checkpoints and what each proves/,/^## Setup, run and test/' BUILDATHON.md | head -60","description":"Read the whole checkpoints section"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2033,"cache_read_input_tokens":956342,"output_tokens":756,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":562},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2033,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":756,"cache_read_input_tokens":956342,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2033,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2033},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cemoi6ViCCL3Wv6skY3dc","type":"assistant","uuid":"76e23bfc-3128-43d0-b5b4-3e402d57abe9","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:39:51.773Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"76e23bfc-3128-43d0-b5b4-3e402d57abe9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"87aba2de-de35-4ff1-9e3a-cbed7d26b95f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XPz7ARpoQEoiomyGftds1v","type":"tool_result","content":"## Checkpoints and what each proves\n\n### The three graft commits carry no checkpoint\n\nState this plainly, because it is the first thing a reviewer checking the trail\nwill notice. These three commits have no checkpoint and never will:\n\n```\nd25e5b51  umbra: initial understanding and intended architecture\n42f215f8  umbra: import the plugin as one commit\n57cea764  umbra: BUILDATHON.md, and restore a deny rule the graft dropped\n```\n\nThey were made by a session running in a different repository. Entire binds a\nsession to the worktree it started in, and the git hooks that write the\n`Entire-Checkpoint` trailer only fire for commits made inside that worktree.\nThese were not, so no hook ran, no trailer was written, and no checkpoint\nexists. `entire doctor` reports nothing wrong, because nothing is: the hooks are\nhealthy and were simply never invoked here.\n\nNothing has been done to paper over that. No prior session was adopted or\nattached, no checkpoint was fabricated for them, and no refs were imported from\nanywhere. A checkpoint is a record that a session produced a commit, and\ninventing one for a commit no session here produced would make the trail a\nworse record than an honest gap. The gap is the record: the work arrived as a\ngraft, and the trail starts after it.\n\n### The checkpoints this session produced\n\nEvery commit below was made in this worktree with hooks live, so each carries\nits own `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer.\n\n| Checkpoint | Commit | What it proves |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bb3270325d86` | `a4b506be` | The fixture baseline. All 16 fixture tests green, which is what makes the probe run's recorded baseline meaningful: a test that was already red cannot be reported as newly broken. |\n| `9a60a142e927` | `6dea614c` | The seeded signature change, and the commit the demo runs against. It is the first commit in this repository with the shape Umbra needs: a parent, a signature change, and a field of dependents that were not all updated. |\n| `fcda6bfff367` | `47bc2411` | The four end to end tests stop resolving against a hash from another repository and resolve against this one, so they run instead of skipping. Also the README reproduce block, re-pointed at this repository and run from a fresh clone. |\n| the commit this table is in | stable state | The intent, architecture, completed work, unresolved work and technical risks as they stand at the deadline. Not tied to a code change; it is the record of where the project actually is. |\n\n### What the trail now demonstrates\n\nThe point of the first two is narrower than it looks, and worth being exact\nabout. Before them, `entire umbra` could not run in this repository at all. The\ndemo claim was a property of commit `0063443` in the repository Umbra was built\nin, and four end to end tests said so out loud by failing to resolve it:\n\n```\n\"0063443\" is neither a checkpoint nor a commit:\ngit rev-parse 0063443 exited 128: fatal: Needed a single revision\n```\n\nRunning against `HEAD` was not a substitute either, for the reason recorded in\nFinding 3: the import commit carries no trailer, so Umbra fell back to pairing\nby session time window and paired with one of the 94 checkpoints that came in\nwith upstream's history, across two unrelated projects.\n\n`9a60a142e927` is the first checkpoint that closes that loop. The commit it\nbelongs to carries its trailer, so the pairing is a fact rather than a guess,\nand the run reproduces the claim exactly: 8 probes selected, 5 cracked, naming\nboth refund tests and the three service tests, with a full sweep and 0 leaks.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7ebe7a03-c343-4b77-bf54-122c6e7164ac","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:39:53.713Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Checkpoints and what each proves\n\n### The three graft commits carry no checkpoint\n\nState this plainly, because it is the first thing a reviewer checking the trail\nwill notice. These three commits have no checkpoint and never will:\n\n```\nd25e5b51  umbra: initial understanding and intended architecture\n42f215f8  umbra: import the plugin as one commit\n57cea764  umbra: BUILDATHON.md, and restore a deny rule the graft dropped\n```\n\nThey were made by a session running in a different repository. Entire binds a\nsession to the worktree it started in, and the git hooks that write the\n`Entire-Checkpoint` trailer only fire for commits made inside that worktree.\nThese were not, so no hook ran, no trailer was written, and no checkpoint\nexists. `entire doctor` reports nothing wrong, because nothing is: the hooks are\nhealthy and were simply never invoked here.\n\nNothing has been done to paper over that. No prior session was adopted or\nattached, no checkpoint was fabricated for them, and no refs were imported from\nanywhere. A checkpoint is a record that a session produced a commit, and\ninventing one for a commit no session here produced would make the trail a\nworse record than an honest gap. The gap is the record: the work arrived as a\ngraft, and the trail starts after it.\n\n### The checkpoints this session produced\n\nEvery commit below was made in this worktree with hooks live, so each carries\nits own `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer.\n\n| Checkpoint | Commit | What it proves |\n|---|---|---|\n| `bb3270325d86` | `a4b506be` | The fixture baseline. All 16 fixture tests green, which is what makes the probe run's recorded baseline meaningful: a test that was already red cannot be reported as newly broken. |\n| `9a60a142e927` | `6dea614c` | The seeded signature change, and the commit the demo runs against. It is the first commit in this repository with the shape Umbra needs: a parent, a signature change, and a field of dependents that were not all updated. |\n| `fcda6bfff367` | `47bc2411` | The four end to end tests stop resolving against a hash from another repository and resolve against this one, so they run instead of skipping. Also the README reproduce block, re-pointed at this repository and run from a fresh clone. |\n| the commit this table is in | stable state | The intent, architecture, completed work, unresolved work and technical risks as they stand at the deadline. Not tied to a code change; it is the record of where the project actually is. |\n\n### What the trail now demonstrates\n\nThe point of the first two is narrower than it looks, and worth being exact\nabout. Before them, `entire umbra` could not run in this repository at all. The\ndemo claim was a property of commit `0063443` in the repository Umbra was built\nin, and four end to end tests said so out loud by failing to resolve it:\n\n```\n\"0063443\" is neither a checkpoint nor a commit:\ngit rev-parse 0063443 exited 128: fatal: Needed a single revision\n```\n\nRunning against `HEAD` was not a substitute either, for the reason recorded in\nFinding 3: the import commit carries no trailer, so Umbra fell back to pairing\nby session time window and paired with one of the 94 checkpoints that came in\nwith upstream's history, across two unrelated projects.\n\n`9a60a142e927` is the first checkpoint that closes that loop. The commit it\nbelongs to carries its trailer, so the pairing is a fact rather than a guess,\nand the run reproduces the claim exactly: 8 probes selected, 5 cracked, naming\nboth refund tests and the three service tests, with a full sweep and 0 leaks.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"76e23bfc-3128-43d0-b5b4-3e402d57abe9","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f