{"parentUuid":"d910f293-8bee-4939-bde3-86f08fa0a0c1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemojXSfwyp8h1wShcnKK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The section is good prose but stale: seven commits now carry no checkpoint, not three, and the table is missing the curveball work. Correcting it."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2014,"cache_read_input_tokens":958375,"output_tokens":2341,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":361},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2014,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":2341,"cache_read_input_tokens":958375,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2014},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CemojLikjPfE7CNN45xb8","type":"assistant","uuid":"ff530eb5-f78f-4e96-bbe8-14cbe81c3fc6","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:40:05.303Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"ff530eb5-f78f-4e96-bbe8-14cbe81c3fc6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemojXSfwyp8h1wShcnKK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015WuGnMohS1nKyqtoAfCoKA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/entire-graph\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport io\np = \"BUILDATHON.md\"; s = io.open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\n\nold_head = \"\"\"### The three graft commits carry no checkpoint\n\nState this plainly, because it is the first thing a reviewer checking the trail\nwill notice. These three commits have no checkpoint and never will:\n\n```\nd25e5b51  umbra: initial understanding and intended architecture\n42f215f8  umbra: import the plugin as one commit\n57cea764  umbra: BUILDATHON.md, and restore a deny rule the graft dropped\n```\n\nThey were made by a session running in a different repository.\"\"\"\n\nnew_head = \"\"\"### Seven commits carry no checkpoint\n\nState this plainly, because it is the first thing a reviewer checking the trail\nwill notice. Seven of the twenty commits on this branch have no checkpoint and\nnever will. They fall into two groups with the same cause.\n\nThe graft:\n\n```\nd25e5b51  umbra: initial understanding and intended architecture\n42f215f8  umbra: import the plugin as one commit\n57cea764  umbra: BUILDATHON.md, and restore a deny rule the graft dropped\n```\n\nThe four fixes made in response to the external review:\n\n```\n1eaad486  umbra: the sweep never reports a false zero\nb4134ca4  umbra: a failed read no longer marks a node lit\n97dd8d7b  umbra: document what the design describes and the binary does not do\ndfefa42e  umbra: record the external review in BUILDATHON.md\n```\n\nAll seven were made by a session running in a different repository.\"\"\"\nassert old_head in s, \"head block not found\"\ns = s.replace(old_head, new_head, 1)\n\nold_tail = \"\"\"These were not, so no hook ran, no trailer was written, and no checkpoint\nexists. `entire doctor` reports nothing wrong, because nothing is: the hooks are\nhealthy and were simply never invoked here.\"\"\"\nnew_tail = \"\"\"These were not, so no hook ran, no trailer was written, and no checkpoint\nexists. `entire doctor` reports nothing wrong, because nothing is: the hooks are\nhealthy and were simply never invoked here.\n\nThat it is the worktree and not the work is easy to show. Later commits in the\nsame session, made once a session was live in this worktree, do carry their\ntrailers: `8a68f3eb`, `10c80da5` and `54caa527` each have one. Same author,\nsame afternoon, same kind of change. The only thing that differed was where the\nsession was bound.\"\"\"\nassert old_tail in s\ns = s.replace(old_tail, new_tail, 1)\n\nold_row = \"\"\"| the commit this table is in | stable state | The intent, architecture, completed work, unresolved work and technical risks as they stand at the deadline. Not tied to a code change; it is the record of where the project actually is. |\"\"\"\nnew_rows = \"\"\"| `21322c5b47f3` | `a49f2ea1` | The intent, architecture, completed work, unresolved work and technical risks as they stood at the pre-noon deadline. Not tied to a code change; it is the record of where the project was. |\n| `819829c9754c` | `3be2edaa` | The curveball plan, written before any code changed, including the required impact analysis on the four graph readers about to change. The tool refused to disambiguate `Dependents` across eight definitions, which is itself the constraint arriving from the tool the phase is about. |\n| `d7859b9ad7ef` | `e41af1db` | Resolution and confidence kept instead of discarded, and the walk carrying the weakest hop along each path. |\n| `4045a5f6a770` | `7744e34a` | The three tiers on every dependent across all four surfaces, as a fourth axis rather than a fifth state. |\n| `a6bcac902c79` | `26ba3d70` | The snapshot's own completeness, warnings and partial failures reported in the graph's codes rather than read past. |\n| `3a8fa1ab19a7` | `4742e272` | The fixture built to contain analysis the graph cannot complete, and the ninth recorded scenario driven from it. |\n| `bb86171b6ee7` | `bcd9e463` | The correction to our own work: only a severe warning promotes a dependent, because promoting on an `info` warning made every node carry the same tier. |\n| `8859dd03469e`, `9086bf442514`, `3837f5eecde4` | `8a68f3eb`, `10c80da5`, `54caa527` | Removing the invented HANDOFF.md, writing the curveball into this document, and pointing the install command at the branch that actually has the code. |\"\"\"\nassert old_row in s\ns = s.replace(old_row, new_rows, 1)\n\nold_intro = \"\"\"Every commit below was made in this worktree with hooks live, so each carries\nits own `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer.\"\"\"\nnew_intro = \"\"\"Thirteen of the twenty commits were made in this worktree with hooks live, so\neach carries its own `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer. Nine distinct checkpoints\ncover them; a checkpoint can span more than one commit when a single session\nproduced several.\"\"\"\nassert old_intro in s\ns = s.replace(old_intro, new_intro, 1)\nio.open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s)\nprint(\"checkpoints section corrected\")\nPY\ngrep -c \"—\" BUILDATHON.md\ncat /tmp/claude-1000/-home-utkuputku-Desktop-Umbra/abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014/scratchpad/install_test.log | tail -3","description":"Correct the checkpoints section"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2014,"cache_read_input_tokens":958375,"output_tokens":2341,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":361},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2014,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":2341,"cache_read_input_tokens":958375,"cache_creation_input_tokens":201