{"parentUuid":"85f314ba-ed67-46fe-b130-b3c6f7c3b1cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemotRUFkrpV4i99q2GzH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both branch and SHA forms fail identically: the module has no tagged version, so Go's deprecation check can't resolve `latest`. `go install` simply doesn't work here. Replacing it with the path I've actually run all day."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1282,"cache_read_input_tokens":962945,"output_tokens":1218,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":430},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1282,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":962945,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1282},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cemot5kqqkiqYa9TpusNc","type":"assistant","uuid":"af895c7e-b866-45a1-ab10-d5b34ef1430e","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:42:07.072Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"af895c7e-b866-45a1-ab10-d5b34ef1430e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CemotRUFkrpV4i99q2GzH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LMMF2TRRDRv6LejqyvvjmW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/utkuputku/entire-graph\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport io\np = \"umbra/README.md\"; s = io.open(p, encoding=\"utf-8\").read()\nold = \"\"\"```\ngo install github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra/cmd/entire-umbra@umbra-buildathon\n```\n\nThe branch is named because Umbra lives on `umbra-buildathon` and not on\n`main`. `main` tracks upstream `entireio/entire-graph` and has no `umbra/`\ndirectory, so `@main` resolves to a path that does not exist. If this work is\never merged to `main`, that suffix can go.\n\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"```\ngit clone -b umbra-buildathon https://github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph\ncd entire-graph/umbra\ngo build -o \"$HOME/.local/bin/entire-umbra\" ./cmd/entire-umbra\n```\n\n**`go install` does not work for this module, and the README used to say it\ndid.** Two things are wrong with the obvious command. `@main` names a branch\nthat has no `umbra/` directory, because `main` tracks upstream\n`entireio/entire-graph`. And naming a branch or a commit that does have it\nstill fails, because the module carries no tagged version:\n\n```\n$ go install github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra/cmd/entire-umbra@umbra-buildathon\ngo: ...loading deprecation for github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra:\n    no matching versions for query \"latest\"\n```\n\nBoth forms were run before this was written. The clone and build above is the\npath every run in this project has actually used.\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s\nio.open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\").write(s.replace(old, new, 1))\nprint(\"install section corrected\")\nPY\nsed -n '55,80p' umbra/README.md; grep -c \"—\" umbra/README.md","description":"Replace go install with the proven clone and build path"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1282,"cache_read_input_tokens":962945,"output_tokens":1218,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":430},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1282,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":962945,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1282},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cemot5kqqkiqYa9TpusNc","type":"assistant","uuid":"a0921b5d-3c51-4214-9b33-b64ff1157510","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:42:14.121Z","effort":"high","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"a0921b5d-3c51-4214-9b33-b64ff1157510","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"87aba2de-de35-4ff1-9e3a-cbed7d26b95f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LMMF2TRRDRv6LejqyvvjmW","type":"tool_result","content":"install section corrected\n## Install\n\n```\ngit clone -b umbra-buildathon https://github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph\ncd entire-graph/umbra\ngo build -o \"$HOME/.local/bin/entire-umbra\" ./cmd/entire-umbra\n```\n\n**`go install` does not work for this module, and the README used to say it\ndid.** Two things are wrong with the obvious command. `@main` names a branch\nthat has no `umbra/` directory, because `main` tracks upstream\n`entireio/entire-graph`. And naming a branch or a commit that does have it\nstill fails, because the module carries no tagged version:\n\n```\n$ go install github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra/cmd/entire-umbra@umbra-buildathon\ngo: ...loading deprecation for github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra:\n    no matching versions for query \"latest\"\n```\n\nBoth forms were run before this was written. The clone and build above is the\npath every run in this project has actually used.\n\nAny executable named `entire-<name>` on `$PATH` is dispatched by the Entire CLI\nkubectl style, so this is all the installation there is. Requires the Entire\nCLI with Checkpoints enabled and the entire-graph plugin.\n0","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5e60c836-a746-40cb-bbcd-885bf3770186","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:42:16.098Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"install section corrected\n## Install\n\n```\ngit clone -b umbra-buildathon https://github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph\ncd entire-graph/umbra\ngo build -o \"$HOME/.local/bin/entire-umbra\" ./cmd/entire-umbra\n```\n\n**`go install` does not work for this module, and the README used to say it\ndid.** Two things are wrong with the obvious command. `@main` names a branch\nthat has no `umbra/` directory, because `main` tracks upstream\n`entireio/entire-graph`. And naming a branch or a commit that does have it\nstill fails, because the module carries no tagged version:\n\n```\n$ go install github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra/cmd/entire-umbra@umbra-buildathon\ngo: ...loading deprecation for github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra:\n    no matching versions for query \"latest\"\n```\n\nBoth forms were run before this was written. The clone and build above is the\npath every run in this project has actually used.\n\nAny executable named `entire-<name>` on `$PATH` is dispatched by the Entire CLI\nkubectl style, so this is all the installation there is. Requires the Entire\nCLI with Checkpoints enabled and the entire-graph plugin.\n0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"returnCodeInterpretation":"No matches found","noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a0921b5d-3c51-4214-9b33-b64ff1157510","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
