{"parentUuid":"7730f3ad-9314-4951-a6b1-54c422ac4e68","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"87aba2de-de35-4ff1-9e3a-cbed7d26b95f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\nThe conversation spans several distinct phases of work on **Umbra**, a plugin for the Entire CLI that finds code an AI agent's change affects but never looked at.\n\n**Phases 14-17 (completed earlier in session):** Finishing prepared scripts, making the scrubber structurally unavoidable, adding known-positive tests, building an eclipse-hero landing page, and doing visual/documentation verification passes.\n\n**Phases 18-21 (UI redesign):** User asked for a designcode.io-inspired UI. After three rejected dark iterations, user demanded complete change; final direction is ink-on-paper editorial.\n\n**Buildathon Track E2 graft (major work):** User gave 10-step instructions to graft Umbra into a fork of `entireio/entire-graph` with an Entire mirror on the India region. **Verbatim security constraints:** \"Do NOT push the old repository's checkpoint refs to the new mirror. The new remote starts clean and stays clean. Do not run entire configure with a checkpoint-remote pointing at the old repo.\" Also: \"No em dashes in anything you write. go test ./... green before every commit.\"\n\n**Most recent task (external review response):** Four tasks, each committed separately, stopping by 14:15 IST:\n1. Fix the sweep's false zero at `umbra/cmd/entire-umbra/execute.go:99` — report \"audit inconclusive\" not `0` when verification is degraded, in terminal/JSON/HTML/packet. Add known-positive test; confirm it fails on revert.\n2. Fix failed reads marking nodes lit at `umbra/internal/transcript/claudecode.go:125` and `:137` — pair tool_use with tool_result, drop reads with `is_error`. Verify demo numbers after. Add fixture test; confirm it fails without fix.\n3. Sync documentation — add a clearly headed README section listing every command/flag the design docs describe that was never built. Scope the Go claim. Handle `--adapter` (prefer rejecting). **The four planning documents stay as written; do NOT edit them to hide the gap.**\n4. Write the review into BUILDATHON.md under known limitations — all ten findings, which two fixed and why, why the rest are documented. Include that five passed `go test`/`go vet` while asserting nothing (same class as Box.Overlaps). \"Do not soften the findings and do not claim anything is fixed that is not.\"\n\n**User's final direction:** \"delete the handoff.md, Go. Commit the dirty tree, then work 1 to 4 in that order.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Entire CLI 0.10.5, entire-graph plugin (built from source with CGO/tree-sitter)\n   - Entire mirrors: `entire repo mirror create <github-url> <cluster-host>`, clusters enumerated via `entire api /api/v1/clusters`; India = `aws-ap-south-1` (jurisdiction `in`)\n   - Graph indexing profiles: `syntax-only` / `fast` / `full`; default is `full` on snapshot and impact, `fast` on search\n   - Umbra's five needed relations: CALLS, USES_TYPE, DATA_FLOWS, TESTS, FILE_CHANGES_WITH\n   - Derived vs parsed relations: TESTS, FILE_CHANGES_WITH, SIMILAR_TO listed for 0 of 185 languages\n   - Four states (lit/penumbra/umbra/unknown), five penumbra tiers\n   - `report.Sealed` choke-point pattern: unexported field, `Seal()` sole constructor\n   - Known-positive testing: every check must be observed failing via mutation\n   - Checkpoint trailers written by git `commit-msg` hook, requires active session bound to that worktree\n   - Semantic diff (`entire graph diff --base X --head Y`) ranking removals-with-dependents above additions\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`umbra/internal/report/model.go`** — Added inconclusive state to `Execution`:\n     ```go\n     // SweepInconclusive is set when the sweep ran but produced no comparable\n     // test ids, so no leak count can be computed.\n     SweepInconclusive bool `json:\"sweep_inconclusive,omitempty\"`\n     SweepInconclusiveReason string `json:\"sweep_inconclusive_reason,omitempty\"`\n     }\n\n     func (e Execution) AuditConclusive() bool {\n         return e.Sweep && !e.SweepInconclusive\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`umbra/cmd/entire-umbra/execute.go`** — In `sweep()`, before computing leaks:\n     ```go\n     if v.Degraded && len(changed) == 0 {\n         a.Execution.SweepInconclusive = true\n         a.Execution.SweepInconclusiveReason = \"the runner printed no per-test ids, so the sweep could not compare any test against the baseline; add -v to the runner\"\n         return nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`umbra/internal/report/table.go`**, **`html.go`**, **`packet.go`** — each gained an inconclusive branch printing \"audit inconclusive\" and never a count.\n\n   - **`umbra/internal/report/seal.go`** — added `x.SweepInconclusiveReason = s.Clean(...)`; also corrected stale comment from \".umbra.json\" to \"--test flag\".\n\n   - **`umbra/internal/report/sweep_inconclusive_test.go`** (new) — three tests: `TestInconclusiveSweepNeverClaimsZeroLeaks`, `TestInconclusiveSweepCarriesItsReason`, `TestCleanSweepStillReportsZeroLeaks`. Checks against `zeroLeakClaims = []string{\"0 leaks\", \"0 leak\", \"**0 leaks**\", \"full sweep, 0\"}`.\n\n   - **`umbra/internal/transcript/claudecode.go`** — added `failedTools := map[string]bool{}` beside `pending`; in the tool_result loop:\n     ```go\n     if b.IsError {\n         failedTools[b.ToolUseID] = true\n         continue\n     }\n     ```\n     and after the scan:\n     ```go\n     if len(failedTools) > 0 {\n         kept := s.Events[:0]\n         for _, ev := range s.Events {\n             if ev.Kind == Read && ev.ToolID != \"\" && failedTools[ev.ToolID] {\n                 continue\n             }\n             kept = append(kept, ev)\n         }\n         s.Events = kept\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **`umbra/internal/transcript/testdata/failed-read.jsonl`** (new) — one successful Read (`ok1`, app/service.py) and one errored Read (`bad1`, app/missing.py with `\"is_error\": true`).\n\n   - **`umbra/internal/transcript/failed_read_test.go`** (new) — `TestFailedReadDoesNotCountAsInspected`, `TestFailedReadLeavesItsFileUnexamined`.\n\n   - **`umbra/README.md`** — added \"## Documented but not built\" section (table of `.umbra.json`, `umbra clean`, `--scrub`, Graph timeouts), \"### Language support is narrower than the design implies\" (Go test selection broken), \"### Flags that are narrower than they look\" (--adapter). Later the Install section was rewritten from `go install ...@main` to clone+build with the failure quoted.\n\n   - **`BUILDATHON.md`** — \"### The external review, and what was done about it\" section under Known limitations; Noon Curveball section (written by another session, committed by me); Checkpoints section corrected from \"three commits carry no checkpoint\" to seven.\n\n   - **`umbra/internal/report/artifacts_all_test.go`** — added `notAPerson()` to exclude service accounts like \"GitHub\" from author-name scanning.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n\n   - **`--clone=false` rejected by gh** — retried without the extra flag; fork created.\n   - **Binary not found after `go install`** — GOBIN pointed at mise directory, not GOPATH/bin. Located at `/home/utkuputku/.local/share/mise/installs/go/1.26.3/bin/entire-graph`.\n   - **NDJSON parse returned zero relations** — my field-name guesses were wrong; inspected real records and found `record_type: \"relation\"` with `from_id`/`to_id`/`type`.\n   - **`TestNoGeneratedArtifactCarriesAnythingPrivate` failed on \"GitHub\"** — the fork's history has a commit authored by \"GitHub\" (web-flow). Added `notAPerson()` filter rather than scrubbing legitimate prose.\n   - **`entire enable` silently removed upstream's `permissions.deny`** — found by semantic diff (2 removals among 2331 additions). Restored the block, kept the hooks.\n   - **Accidentally rewrote `site/self/umbra.html`** (a generated report artifact) because my exclusion regex anchored on `./` but grep emitted paths without it. Restored from source repo, verified all 7 artifacts byte-identical.\n   - **Sticky topbar broken twice** — first by `umbra.css`'s `overflow-x: hidden` on html/body, then by a rule listing `.topbar` among elements made `position: relative`. Added a comment explaining why the bar is excluded.\n   - **14px horizontal overflow at 390px** — three wrong guesses (grain, ticker, phase rows) before bisecting in the browser found `.head::before` scrim at `min(880px, 118%)`.\n   - **`.bar` class collision** — umbra.css owns `.bar { height: 22px }` for the report's score bar; my header inherited it and was 32px tall with nav overflowing, putting a rule through the words. Renamed to `.topbar-inner`.\n   - **Corona drift desynced the map** — animating the whole corona SVG scaled the occluding disc while the map didn't move. Changed to animate only `.corona-field`.\n   - **`go install` fails entirely for this module** — both `@umbra-buildathon` and an explicit SHA fail with `loading deprecation for github.com/u7k4rs6/entire-graph/umbra: no matching versions for query \"latest\"`. My first \"fix\" (changing `@main` to `@umbra-buildathon`) was itself unverified. Replaced with clone+build.\n\n   **User feedback that changed direction:**\n   - \"this is the shitties website i've ever seen. As i said, change it whole\" and \"especially the map, looks soooo bad\" — led to abandoning three dark iterations for an ink-on-paper inversion and turning off all map glow layers.\n   - \"noooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo, i don't want threeui' clone. This contains libraries.\" — I had started cloning threeui's site chrome (sidebar); reverted and went into their component catalogue instead.\n   - \"don't just build the doc, make the whole site\" — led to six pages instead of one long page.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n   - Established the demo claim (8 selected, 5 cracked, 0 leaks) is a property of commit `0063443` in the source repo; not reproducible in the fork until the fixture change was seeded there.\n   - Diagnosed that `entire umbra HEAD` paired with an unrelated upstream checkpoint by session-time window and tried to read a 3.4M-token transcript.\n   - **Declined to rewrite commit timestamps** when asked to backdate them to 11am \"randomly\" — it would falsify submission evidence and break the checkpoint trail (5 commits bind checkpoints to SHAs).\n   - Confirmed the private `u7k4rs6/Umbra` repo doesn't affect the submission: the fork is public, no submitted doc links to it, and keeping it private is correct because its checkpoint refs hold another project's transcripts.\n   - Verified `--adapter` already rejects unsupported values, so recorded the review as wrong on that point rather than \"fixing\" working code.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"anything left?\"\n   - \"You are in the Umbra repo (phase 14 complete, 316 tests green, clean tree). Read umbra/NOTES.md, umbra/docs/SECURITY_AND_ACCESS.md, and every call site of the scrubber before changing anything. Two tasks. No redesign, no frontend changes, no reopening settled decisions. [1. Make the scrubber the only exit... 2. Known-positive tests for every check...] Also fix scripts/checkpoint-refs-audit.sh itself...\"\n   - \"You are in the Umbra repo (phase 16 complete...). Read umbra/docs/FRONTEND_SPEC.md in full... [phase 16 eclipse hero spec with `<FONT DECISION GOES HERE>` placeholder]\"\n   - \"You are in ~/entire-graph on branch umbra-buildathon... [phase 17 two visual checks, PUBLISH.md, README pass]\"\n   - \"i want to see it live, is it anywhere on local host?\"\n   - \"https://designcode.io/ check out this website. I want this UI. It's dynamic, interactive, and looks cool. Change it acc to yourself. You have literal 6 hrs to do that on autopilot. The problem is, it has generic fonts and colour scheme. You have to fix it too\"\n   - \"try using plawright always. It's better if you visually check and build stuff\"\n   - \"still it's the same\"\n   - \"i asked you to clone that website and then customize it. what have you done?\"\n   - \"i you havn't , get started\"\n   - \"i you want any help in resources, https://threeui.com/browse check this out, it has a crazy library. All you have to aim is, to make the site look the coolest shit judges will ever see.\"\n   - \"don't just build the doc, make the whole site\"\n   - \"try to make it interactive, like hovering effects, cursor trailing effects, and more\"\n   - \"utilize whole 6 hrs, and make the best you can, keep rechecking it. and i want you to be active again and again, fine tuning stuff for straight 6 hrs. Don't get completed before that\"\n   - \"this is the shitties website i've ever seen. As i said , change it whole\"\n   - \"especially the map, looks soooo bad\"\n   - \"noooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo, i don't want threeui' clone. This contains libraries. Use some of them to make a good ui. Go inside the site and browse some stuff\"\n   - \".Track: E2, Graph Intelligence. Upstream is entireio/entire-graph on main (public, MIT). Umbra lives in umbra/ as its own Go module and never imports entire-graph packages. **Do NOT push the old repository's checkpoint refs to the new mirror. The new remote starts clean and stays clean. Do not run entire configure with a checkpoint-remote pointing at the old repo.** No em dashes in anything you write. go test ./... green before every commit. [STEPS 1-10 covering mirror workflow, plugin install, field verification, first commit, second commit, graph evidence, BUILDATHON.md, checkpoints, final push]\"\n   - \"login is completed\"\n   - \"You are in ~/entire-graph on branch umbra-buildathon, hooks live, tree clean. Read umbra/NOTES.md and umbra/BUILDATHON.md first. An external review found ten issues. You are fixing two of them in code, correcting the docs, and recording the rest honestly. Do NOT attempt the other issues; time is short and a rushed fix to test selection is worse than a documented gap. No em dashes. go test ./... green before every commit. Commit each of the four tasks separately with an Entire-Checkpoint trailer. Stop by 14:15 IST regardless of where you are, so the tree is clean and pushed before submission. [tasks 1-4 in full]\"\n   - \"what are the timings of commits?\"\n   - \"if someone sees this project, what is the earliest commit they'll see\"\n   - \"my umbra on github is priv, will it effect anything?\"\n   - \"then what's left now?\"\n   - \"delete the handoff.md, Go. Commit the dirty tree, then work 1 to 4 in that order.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Push the branch** — `umbra-buildathon` had unpushed commits before my last batch; needs `git push origin umbra-buildathon`.\n   - Report final state: demo numbers after fix 2, the two known-positive tests with revert proof, final test count, commit SHA to submit.\n   - Open question raised but unanswered: whether to open a PR from `umbra-buildathon` into `main` (main is a protected branch; push to it was rejected).\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Immediately before this summary, I had just completed items 3 and 4 of the user's ordered list (\"Commit the dirty tree, then work 1 to 4 in that order\") and committed them together.\n\n   The final command staged `umbra/README.md` and `BUILDATHON.md` and committed with message \"umbra: correct the install path and the checkpoint trail\", covering two documentation claims found wrong by checking rather than reading:\n   - `go install` does not work for this module at all (both `@umbra-buildathon` and explicit SHA fail with `no matching versions for query \"latest\"`), so README now gives clone+build and quotes the failure. The commit message explicitly admits: \"The first fix committed an hour ago was itself unverified.\"\n   - The checkpoints section said three commits carry no checkpoint; seven do (three graft + four review-response commits). Thirteen of twenty commits carry trailers, covered by nine checkpoints.\n\n   The command output confirmed:\n   ```\n   exit=0\n   (blank=clean)\n   ALL GREEN\n   ```\n\n   So the tree is clean and `go test ./...` passes all packages. Commits made this session in order: `bcd9e463` (severe warnings only promote), `8a68f3eb` (remove HANDOFF.md), `10c80da5` (write the noon curveball into BUILDATHON.md), `54caa527` (point install command at branch), and the final combined install-path/checkpoint-trail commit.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Push the branch and report the final state, which is what the user's original brief required: \"Then: push, confirm the branch is up to date, and report with the demo numbers after fix 2, the two known-positive tests and proof each fails without its fix, the final test count, and the commit SHA to submit.\" The user's most recent instruction was \"delete the handoff.md, Go. Commit the dirty tree, then work 1 to 4 in that order\" — all of which is now complete with a clean tree and green tests, so the remaining step is the push and final report. Deadline is 14:15 IST; last time check was 13:28 IST.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/utkuputku/.claude/projects/-home-utkuputku-Desktop-Umbra/8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"c5525b94-4fe7-4d39-850b-df6b43cab0ef","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:45:03.811Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"c5525b94-4fe7-4d39-850b-df6b43cab0ef","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/home/utkuputku/entire-graph/BUILDATHON.md","displayPath":"../../entire-graph/BUILDATHON.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"30bdf5f3-3a77-41bf-b139-5e7696608266","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:45:04.159Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"30bdf5f3-3a77-41bf-b139-5e7696608266","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/utkuputku/entire-graph/umbra/KICKOFF_PROMPT.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/utkuputku/entire-graph/umbra/KICKOFF_PROMPT.md","content":"# Kickoff prompt\n\nThis is the brief Umbra was built from, recorded here because the build never\nkept it as a file. It is reconstructed from the session record rather than\ncopied from an existing document, and it is placed in the first commit so the\nintent is in the repository before any code is.\n\n## The problem\n\nFind the code an AI agent's change affects but the agent never looked at.\n\nA clean diff and a confident description tell a reviewer what changed. They do\nnot tell the reviewer what the agent never opened. Umbra takes the dependents of\nevery changed symbol from Entire Graph, subtracts what the session actually\nexamined according to the checkpoint's tool activity and the agent's own words,\nranks what is left in shadow, runs the tests that reach it, and then sweeps the\nwhole suite once so the selection audits itself.\n\n## Settled decisions, not open questions\n\n- Go, one static binary named `entire-umbra`, dispatched by the Entire CLI\n  kubectl style. Its own Go module under `umbra/`.\n- Inputs come only through documented Entire and Graph output. No scraping of\n  internal state, no undocumented files.\n- Four boundaries behind interfaces, and exactly one Runner for external\n  processes, so tests replay recorded fixtures.\n- **No model anywhere in Umbra.** The core is deterministic and offline.\n- Four states: lit, penumbra, umbra, unknown, with five penumbra tiers.\n- Missing data is a state, never an error. A transcript with no tool records\n  gives every node `unknown`, which is the correct answer rather than a guess.\n- **Umbra never executes commands from a transcript.** Test ids are validated\n  against a strict pattern and passed as separate argv elements. There is no\n  `sh -c` anywhere in it.\n- Layout is computed in Go and written into the report JSON. The browser never\n  computes positions, only styles and states.\n- Vanilla JavaScript and CSS for the report and the site. No libraries, no\n  fonts fetched, no network requests, no motion on load in the report.\n- No em dashes in any file, code comments included.\n- Tests replay recorded fixtures. No test may need a live agent or a network.\n- `go test ./...` green at every commit. Commit after every phase, never squash.\n- Touch nothing outside `umbra/` except a one line pointer in the repository\n  README.\n- Run `entire graph impact` before changing a file the build did not create.\n- Keep the machine light: one agent session, no parallel builds, no background\n  processes left running.\n\n## What the reviewer is meant to get\n\nAn eclipse map that can be replayed in the order the agent looked at things,\nplus a one page packet a reviewer reads in a minute, plus an exit code a CI job\ncan act on.\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}},"displayPath":"../../entire-graph/umbra/KICKOFF_PROMPT.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2871153a-9795-4223-bcbf-67b5875e3768","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:45:03.835Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
{"parentUuid":"2871153a-9795-4223-bcbf-67b5875e3768","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-utkuputku-Desktop-Umbra/abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014/scratchpad/serve.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-utkuputku-Desktop-Umbra/abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014/scratchpad/serve.py","content":"# A local preview server for umbra/site that refuses to be cached.\n#\n# python -m http.server sends Last-Modified and no Cache-Control, so a browser\n# heuristically holds on to the stylesheet and the scripts, and a reload shows\n# the old page even though the server is handing out the new one. This sends\n# no-store on everything.\nimport http.server\nimport socketserver\n\nROOT = \"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra/umbra/site\"\nPORT = 8412\n\n\nclass NoCache(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler):\n    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        super().__init__(*args, directory=ROOT, **kwargs)\n\n    def end_headers(self):\n        self.send_header(\"Cache-Control\", \"no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, max-age=0\")\n        self.send_header(\"Pragma\", \"no-cache\")\n        self.send_header(\"Expires\", \"0\")\n        super().end_headers()\n\n    def log_message(self, format, *args):\n        pass\n\n\nsocketserver.TCPServer.allow_reuse_address = True\nwith socketserver.TCPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", PORT), NoCache) as httpd:\n    print(\"serving umbra/site on http://127.0.0.1:%d/ with caching off\" % PORT)\n    httpd.serve_forever()\n","numLines":32,"startLine":1,"totalLines":32}},"displayPath":"../../../../tmp/claude-1000/-home-utkuputku-Desktop-Umbra/abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014/scratchpad/serve.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fb8f88c6-c1de-4e22-bfb2-604aead3f281","timestamp":"2026-09-06T07:45:03.835Z","session_id":"abbf9c0c-4f5e-46cd-a7be-70d09966a014","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/utkuputku/Desktop/Umbra","sessionId":"8017734d-cdf6-4a18-b2f8-f4b5f637ec35","version":"2.1.261","gitBranch":"main","slug":"twinkling-waddling-dragon"}
